{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T21:32:52.369Z","ordinal":9463,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_068dffc2438c6825016a8cb87c3c1c87d0aef900316bfc0262","status":"completed","call_id":"call_BgSqKRnNX2pNINgX7OqXhNdI","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor-design.md\\n@@\\n worktree bootstraps only from verified untracked, non-symlinked runtime evidence\\n inside that exact worktree or from an explicit `entire enable` run in that\\n worktree. A tracked `core.hooksPath` inside the worktree is never activation\\n evidence.\\n+\\n+Accepted worktree-specific legacy evidence is intentionally exact:\\n+\\n+- a session-state record in `<git-common-dir>/entire-sessions` whose canonical\\n+  `WorktreePath` and `WorktreeID` both identify this worktree; or\\n+- at least one regular, untracked, non-symlinked recognized runtime file beneath\\n+  `.entire/metadata/<session-id>/` (`prompt.txt`, `full.jsonl`, `full.log`,\\n+  `transcript.jsonl`, `metadata.json`, `checkpoint.json`, or\\n+  `content_hash.txt`).\\n+\\n+Empty directories, logs, tmp files, project settings, shared/common hooks, and\\n+any external or worktree-relative `core.hooksPath` are not bootstrap evidence.\\n@@\\n Local settings paths are rejected as locally owned if the file or any parent\\n path component traverses a symlink. Tracked, unreadable, malformed, or\\n unverifiable local configuration fails toward the untrusted classification.\\n Local activation does not relax existing per-field provenance checks: in\\n particular, a project-file `opf_command` remains rejected after `entire enable`.\\n+Symlink validation starts from the canonical worktree root and inspects only the\\n+worktree-relative `.entire/settings*.json` components with `lstat`; it does not\\n+reject a worktree merely because the caller reached the worktree root through a\\n+platform alias such as macOS `/var` -> `/private/var`.\\n@@\\n - Enabling a main worktree does not locally activate a newly added sibling that\\n   contains committed `enabled: true` settings.\\n+- Legacy bootstrap accepts only the enumerated per-worktree record/file shapes;\\n+  an external `core.hooksPath` is insufficient even in a single-worktree repo.\\n+- Enable-after-uninstall selects the worktree route with global policy off and\\n+  the git-common route with global policy on, replacing the disabled tombstone\\n+  in both cases.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a035a3-086c-7020-a149-5e66cf01e9bf","create_time":1787607160.156694}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T21:32:52.492Z","ordinal":9464,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a025ce-e754-7631-8467-eaa6035ba0f8","turn_id":"01a035a3-086c-7020-a149-5e66cf01e9bf","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-9fd904cf-82cd-4b11-b4f1-0df7a0650e05","changes":{"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor-design.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -183,2 +183,14 @@\n \n+Accepted worktree-specific legacy evidence is intentionally exact:\n+\n+- a session-state record in `<git-common-dir>/entire-sessions` whose canonical\n+  `WorktreePath` and `WorktreeID` both identify this worktree; or\n+- at least one regular, untracked, non-symlinked recognized runtime file beneath\n+  `.entire/metadata/<session-id>/` (`prompt.txt`, `full.jsonl`, `full.log`,\n+  `transcript.jsonl`, `metadata.json`, `checkpoint.json`, or\n+  `content_hash.txt`).\n+\n+Empty directories, logs, tmp files, project settings, shared/common hooks, and\n+any external or worktree-relative `core.hooksPath` are not bootstrap evidence.\n+\n A repository-level `enabled: false` may remain an explicit capture veto. An\n@@ -215,2 +227,6 @@\n particular, a project-file `opf_command` remains rejected after `entire enable`.\n+Symlink validation starts from the canonical worktree root and inspects only the\n+worktree-relative `.entire/settings*.json` components with `lstat`; it does not\n+reject a worktree merely because the caller reached the worktree root through a\n+platform alias such as macOS `/var` -> `/private/var`.\n \n@@ -481,2 +497,7 @@\n   contains committed `enabled: true` settings.\n+- Legacy bootstrap accepts only the enumerated per-worktree record/file shapes;\n+  an external `core.hooksPath` is insufficient even in a single-worktree repo.\n+- Enable-after-uninstall selects the worktree route with global policy off and\n+  the git-common route with global policy on, replacing the disabled tombstone\n+  in both cases.\n - Route-resolution failure skips capture without failing the host operation.\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor-design.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1787607172425,"completed_at_ms":1787607172492}}
