{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T21:42:30.575Z","ordinal":9597,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_01a035b9-97af-75e3-8b07-6fa7a1e0f763","role":"user","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"okay question, does this refactor keep all the behavior we have the same as we have now?"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a035b9-9495-73f2-bd24-2ae6dcab41a9","create_time":1787607750.575676}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T21:42:30.576Z","ordinal":9598,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a025ce-e754-7631-8467-eaa6035ba0f8","turn_id":"01a035b9-9495-73f2-bd24-2ae6dcab41a9","item":{"type":"UserMessage","id":"01a035b9-97b0-7ea3-9d3a-4f8227249068","content":[{"type":"text","text":"okay question, does this refactor keep all the behavior we have the same as we have now?","text_elements":[]}]},"started_at_ms":1787607750576,"completed_at_ms":1787607750576}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T21:42:38.983Z","ordinal":9599,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a025ce-e754-7631-8467-eaa6035ba0f8","turn_id":"01a035b9-9495-73f2-bd24-2ae6dcab41a9","item":{"type":"Reasoning","id":"rs_068dffc2438c6825016a8cbaccb2e887d0b0a7dba6d63c3521","summary_text":[],"raw_content":[]},"started_at_ms":1787607756715,"completed_at_ms":1787607758982}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T21:42:38.987Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"id":"rs_068dffc2438c6825016a8cbaccb2e887d0b0a7dba6d63c3521","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a035b9-9495-73f2-bd24-2ae6dcab41a9"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T21:42:47.475Z","ordinal":9601,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a025ce-e754-7631-8467-eaa6035ba0f8","turn_id":"01a035b9-9495-73f2-bd24-2ae6dcab41a9","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_068dffc2438c6825016a8cbacef74887d0b275944b299ae11f","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"No—not every current behavior. The refactor preserves the feature’s intended capabilities, but deliberately removes or changes several user-facing mechanisms.\n\nPreserved:\n\n- Global tracking activates repositories automatically.\n- Explicitly enabled repositories continue tracking when global tracking is off.\n- Runtime data and hooks remain invisible to `git status`.\n- Linked worktrees remain independently trackable.\n- Exclusions, trust checks, checkpointing, status, doctor, and supported agent integrations remain.\n- Existing local repositories receive a compatibility migration based on real local activation evidence.\n\nIntentionally changed:\n\n- Global configuration becomes settings-file-only.\n- `entire enable --global` and `entire disable --global` disappear.\n- The ask-once global-enable wizard disappears.\n- `entire trust` and `entire trust --revoke` disappear; trust is edited in settings.\n- The pre-push trust prompt disappears. Untrusted egress is held non-interactively with a concise message.\n- User-level Claude/Gemini hooks are installed as inert infrastructure rather than being tied to global-enable commands.\n- Unused Gemini hook events are removed.\n- Once a worktree chooses its runtime location, that route stays fixed instead of being migrated later.\n\nSo the goal is behavioral equivalence for tracking, isolation, safety, and diagnostics—not command-for-command compatibility. The deleted behaviors are the redundant parts that made the merged stack feel stitched together. No production code has been changed yet."}],"phase":"final_answer"},"started_at_ms":1787607758988,"completed_at_ms":1787607767475}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T21:42:47.479Z","ordinal":9602,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_068dffc2438c6825016a8cbacef74887d0b275944b299ae11f","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"No—not every current behavior. The refactor preserves the feature’s intended capabilities, but deliberately removes or changes several user-facing mechanisms.\n\nPreserved:\n\n- Global tracking activates repositories automatically.\n- Explicitly enabled repositories continue tracking when global tracking is off.\n- Runtime data and hooks remain invisible to `git status`.\n- Linked worktrees remain independently trackable.\n- Exclusions, trust checks, checkpointing, status, doctor, and supported agent integrations remain.\n- Existing local repositories receive a compatibility migration based on real local activation evidence.\n\nIntentionally changed:\n\n- Global configuration becomes settings-file-only.\n- `entire enable --global` and `entire disable --global` disappear.\n- The ask-once global-enable wizard disappears.\n- `entire trust` and `entire trust --revoke` disappear; trust is edited in settings.\n- The pre-push trust prompt disappears. Untrusted egress is held non-interactively with a concise message.\n- User-level Claude/Gemini hooks are installed as inert infrastructure rather than being tied to global-enable commands.\n- Unused Gemini hook events are removed.\n- Once a worktree chooses its runtime location, that route stays fixed instead of being migrated later.\n\nSo the goal is behavioral equivalence for tracking, isolation, safety, and diagnostics—not command-for-command compatibility. The deleted behaviors are the redundant parts that made the merged stack feel stitched together. No production code has been changed yet."}],"phase":"final_answer","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a035b9-9495-73f2-bd24-2ae6dcab41a9","create_time":1787607751.070317}}}
