{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T21:45:07.581Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"id":"rs_068dffc2438c6825016a8cbb5f325487d09aad25bc85f8a90e","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a035bb-e411-7b32-a380-13e06970de42"},"summary":[],"type":"reasoning"}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T21:45:10.479Z","ordinal":9612,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a025ce-e754-7631-8467-eaa6035ba0f8","turn_id":"01a035bb-e411-7b32-a380-13e06970de42","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_068dffc2438c6825016a8cbb638ce487d0b1f0760b9f4c9810","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"You’re right—the refactor scope should be narrower. I treated adjacent trust and agent-hook cleanup as removable redundancy, but those are product behaviors that must survive; only global-enable configuration should lose its CLI/wizard mutation paths.\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\nA consolidation refactor should preserve externally observable behavior unless a change is explicitly part of the requirement. Here, “settings-only” constrains global-enable configuration; it does not authorize redesigning egress consent or agent lifecycle coverage.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\nI’m revising the local design accordingly: preserve pre-push trust, egress enforcement, and Claude/Gemini behavior while still fixing their reported correctness and safety findings."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1787607907582,"completed_at_ms":1787607910478}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T21:45:10.481Z","ordinal":9613,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_068dffc2438c6825016a8cbb638ce487d0b1f0760b9f4c9810","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"You’re right—the refactor scope should be narrower. I treated adjacent trust and agent-hook cleanup as removable redundancy, but those are product behaviors that must survive; only global-enable configuration should lose its CLI/wizard mutation paths.\n\n`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\nA consolidation refactor should preserve externally observable behavior unless a change is explicitly part of the requirement. Here, “settings-only” constrains global-enable configuration; it does not authorize redesigning egress consent or agent lifecycle coverage.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\nI’m revising the local design accordingly: preserve pre-push trust, egress enforcement, and Claude/Gemini behavior while still fixing their reported correctness and safety findings."}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a035bb-e411-7b32-a380-13e06970de42","create_time":1787607902.740111}}}
