{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T21:46:23.217Z","ordinal":9672,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_068dffc2438c6825016a8cbbabd2d087d08059fdcb1d92160e","status":"completed","call_id":"call_lwo7GLlbzjha9XDBi1NcMTYT","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor-design.md\\n@@\\n-Gemini hooks whose parser always returns no lifecycle event are not installed:\\n-`AfterModel`, `BeforeToolSelection`, `BeforeTool`, `AfterTool`, and\\n-`Notification`.\\n+The declarative specification preserves the complete existing event set and\\n+command behavior. In particular, Gemini continues installing all twelve current\\n+entries: `SessionStart`, both `SessionEnd` matchers, `BeforeAgent`, `AfterAgent`,\\n+`BeforeModel`, `AfterModel`, `BeforeToolSelection`, `BeforeTool`, `AfterTool`,\\n+`PreCompress`, and `Notification`. Events that currently parse to no lifecycle\\n+event remain installed because their presence is part of the supported Gemini\\n+integration contract. Claude Code likewise preserves its current lifecycle and\\n+tool-use matcher coverage. The refactor deduplicates how these entries are\\n+declared and reconciled; it does not prune or reinterpret them.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a035bb-e411-7b32-a380-13e06970de42","create_time":1787607979.101096}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T21:46:23.331Z","ordinal":9673,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a025ce-e754-7631-8467-eaa6035ba0f8","turn_id":"01a035bb-e411-7b32-a380-13e06970de42","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-4d8927fa-ca45-432d-b25c-92cf29a89edd","changes":{"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor-design.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -423,5 +423,11 @@\n \n-Gemini hooks whose parser always returns no lifecycle event are not installed:\n-`AfterModel`, `BeforeToolSelection`, `BeforeTool`, `AfterTool`, and\n-`Notification`.\n+The declarative specification preserves the complete existing event set and\n+command behavior. In particular, Gemini continues installing all twelve current\n+entries: `SessionStart`, both `SessionEnd` matchers, `BeforeAgent`, `AfterAgent`,\n+`BeforeModel`, `AfterModel`, `BeforeToolSelection`, `BeforeTool`, `AfterTool`,\n+`PreCompress`, and `Notification`. Events that currently parse to no lifecycle\n+event remain installed because their presence is part of the supported Gemini\n+integration contract. Claude Code likewise preserves its current lifecycle and\n+tool-use matcher coverage. The refactor deduplicates how these entries are\n+declared and reconciled; it does not prune or reinterpret them.\n Legacy user/repository hook forms are normalized during foreground\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor-design.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1787607983263,"completed_at_ms":1787607983331}}
