{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T21:46:36.505Z","ordinal":9678,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_068dffc2438c6825016a8cbbb0c39c87d09429491bcf979d8f","status":"completed","call_id":"call_dGvMw1cRqxRnIntb6TBJJvBS","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor-design.md\\n@@\\n-| `01M0TSFS8WSCD7CNSV5XJ4Q983` — migration gate blocks behind prompt/condensation | Remove migration gate and interactive trust prompt | Pending and non-pending pre-push cases never read stdin; non-pending is silent; pending emits one line; concurrent hook and push do not block |\\n+| `01M0TSFS8WSCD7CNSV5XJ4Q983` — migration gate blocks behind prompt/condensation | Remove the takeover migration gate; keep the trust prompt outside route-selection locking | Non-pending pre-push is silent; pending interactive pre-push prompts through `/dev/tty`; concurrent hook and push do not block on route selection |\\n@@\\n-| `01M0TSDJQKTMR26TPV0Z1N7YG8` — accessible prompt auto-grants or panics | Remove pre-push trust prompt | `ACCESSIBLE=1` pre-push remains non-interactive, held, and panic-free |\\n+| `01M0TSDJQKTMR26TPV0Z1N7YG8` — accessible prompt auto-grants or panics | Preserve the prompt but require an explicit supported selection; otherwise hold | `ACCESSIBLE=1` never grants the default implicitly, never consumes Git stdin, and never panics; explicit selections retain Yes/Not now/Always semantics |\\n@@\\n-| `01M0TSEY7XNH32BR7ZXEGEMABS` — revoke misses stale origin after identity flip | Remove trust writers/revoke; use pure current-identity matching over explicit settings | Origin→path→origin and multiple fetch/push URL cases authorize only when every current key is explicitly trusted |\\n+| `01M0TSEY7XNH32BR7ZXEGEMABS` — revoke misses stale origin after identity flip | Preserve trust/revoke and record the exact keys written by each CLI/prompt grant so later re-grant/revoke can remove its stale identities without deleting hand-authored entries | Origin→path→origin, path→origin→path, and multiple fetch/push URL cases leave only the intended grant and revoke every recorded identity |\\n@@\\n-Two older GitHub comments are also covered: the removed prompt can no longer\\n-misstate folder-versus-origin scope, and the remaining hold message is exactly\\n-one line.\\n+Two older GitHub comments are also covered: the preserved prompt derives its\\n+folder-versus-origin label from the same identity used by the gate and writer,\\n+and the hold message remains concise and actionable.\\n@@\\n-- Gemini no-op lifecycle hooks are absent.\\n+- Claude Code and all twelve current Gemini entries remain present with the same\\n+  command forms, matchers, deduplication, and event behavior.\\n@@\\n-- Accessible mode cannot grant consent or consume pre-push stdin because the\\n-  prompt is absent.\\n+- Accessible mode cannot grant consent implicitly or consume pre-push stdin;\\n+  explicit Yes/Not now/Always choices retain their current effects.\\n@@\\n-2. untrusted pending checkpoint -> successful branch push plus one-line hold;\\n-3. settings-file origin/path trust -> queued checkpoint drain;\\n+2. untrusted pending checkpoint -> interactive Yes/Not now/Always behavior,\\n+   plus non-interactive successful branch push with held checkpoints;\\n+3. `entire trust`, pre-push trust, and settings-file origin/path trust -> queued\\n+   checkpoint drain;\\n@@\\n-### Keep interactive trust while making activation settings-only\\n-\\n-This retains a convenient consent prompt but violates the requirement that the\\n-global block is writable only through the settings file. It also preserves the\\n-accessible-mode stdin hazard and keeps human input inside pre-push execution.\\n+### Remove interactive trust while making activation settings-only\\n+\\n+This would simplify pre-push, but it would regress an intentional consent flow\\n+and force users to leave their push to configure egress. The chosen design keeps\\n+the prompt, isolates it from route-selection locks and Git stdin, and fixes the\\n+accessible-mode behavior without removing the feature.\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a035bb-e411-7b32-a380-13e06970de42","create_time":1787607983.910253}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T21:46:36.618Z","ordinal":9679,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a025ce-e754-7631-8467-eaa6035ba0f8","turn_id":"01a035bb-e411-7b32-a380-13e06970de42","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-515679d3-d0f6-4b96-a3af-37d02e40d99e","changes":{"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor-design.md":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -497,3 +497,3 @@\n | --- | --- | --- |\n-| `01M0TSFS8WSCD7CNSV5XJ4Q983` — migration gate blocks behind prompt/condensation | Remove migration gate and interactive trust prompt | Pending and non-pending pre-push cases never read stdin; non-pending is silent; pending emits one line; concurrent hook and push do not block |\n+| `01M0TSFS8WSCD7CNSV5XJ4Q983` — migration gate blocks behind prompt/condensation | Remove the takeover migration gate; keep the trust prompt outside route-selection locking | Non-pending pre-push is silent; pending interactive pre-push prompts through `/dev/tty`; concurrent hook and push do not block on route selection |\n | `01M0TSFQ9D1EH7M7VCZ43FYVC6` — gate failure aborts commit/push/session | Remove gate; policy/route failures skip Entire work | Separate forced-failure tests prove commit, push, and agent-session host operations succeed; local OPF safety failure still aborts push |\n@@ -501,10 +501,10 @@\n | `01M0TSE2YQG4NHX4HQPK7P7FW6` — symlinked `.entire` bypasses executable-setting trust | Reject symlink-traversing local settings and use an explicit hook-time field whitelist | Real clone fixture with tracked `.entire` symlink plus malicious OPF, checkpoint destination, external-agent, hook-path, and strategy values cannot influence hook execution or egress |\n-| `01M0TSDJQKTMR26TPV0Z1N7YG8` — accessible prompt auto-grants or panics | Remove pre-push trust prompt | `ACCESSIBLE=1` pre-push remains non-interactive, held, and panic-free |\n+| `01M0TSDJQKTMR26TPV0Z1N7YG8` — accessible prompt auto-grants or panics | Preserve the prompt but require an explicit supported selection; otherwise hold | `ACCESSIBLE=1` never grants the default implicitly, never consumes Git stdin, and never panics; explicit selections retain Yes/Not now/Always semantics |\n | `01M0TSGCWR0EVVQWK526A4BTEZ` — already-expired try-lock context | Remove try-lock and takeover migration | Barrier-controlled concurrent route-selection test proves both callers return the same complete winner and local enable records activation separately |\n-| `01M0TSEY7XNH32BR7ZXEGEMABS` — revoke misses stale origin after identity flip | Remove trust writers/revoke; use pure current-identity matching over explicit settings | Origin→path→origin and multiple fetch/push URL cases authorize only when every current key is explicitly trusted |\n+| `01M0TSEY7XNH32BR7ZXEGEMABS` — revoke misses stale origin after identity flip | Preserve trust/revoke and record the exact keys written by each CLI/prompt grant so later re-grant/revoke can remove its stale identities without deleting hand-authored entries | Origin→path→origin, path→origin→path, and multiple fetch/push URL cases leave only the intended grant and revoke every recorded identity |\n | `01M0TSGEJB4B513AV3TS310RN0` — disable message contradicts `trust_all` | Remove global disable command; require active policy in egress decision | Disabled global tier is inactive even with `trust_all: true` |\n \n-Two older GitHub comments are also covered: the removed prompt can no longer\n-misstate folder-versus-origin scope, and the remaining hold message is exactly\n-one line.\n+Two older GitHub comments are also covered: the preserved prompt derives its\n+folder-versus-origin label from the same identity used by the gate and writer,\n+and the hold message remains concise and actionable.\n \n@@ -551,3 +551,4 @@\n - Agent hook specifications drive install, recognition, removal, and count.\n-- Gemini no-op lifecycle hooks are absent.\n+- Claude Code and all twelve current Gemini entries remain present with the same\n+  command forms, matchers, deduplication, and event behavior.\n - Committed and symlinked repository settings cannot activate executable\n@@ -558,4 +559,4 @@\n   untrusted secondary URL holds egress.\n-- Accessible mode cannot grant consent or consume pre-push stdin because the\n-  prompt is absent.\n+- Accessible mode cannot grant consent implicitly or consume pre-push stdin;\n+  explicit Yes/Not now/Always choices retain their current effects.\n - `status`, `help`, `version`, `auth token`, and JSON inspection commands create\n@@ -568,4 +569,6 @@\n 1. settings-file enable -> agent hook activity -> hidden capture;\n-2. untrusted pending checkpoint -> successful branch push plus one-line hold;\n-3. settings-file origin/path trust -> queued checkpoint drain;\n+2. untrusted pending checkpoint -> interactive Yes/Not now/Always behavior,\n+   plus non-interactive successful branch push with held checkpoints;\n+3. `entire trust`, pre-push trust, and settings-file origin/path trust -> queued\n+   checkpoint drain;\n 4. explicit enable after global capture -> same runtime route and continuous\n@@ -617,7 +620,8 @@\n \n-### Keep interactive trust while making activation settings-only\n+### Remove interactive trust while making activation settings-only\n \n-This retains a convenient consent prompt but violates the requirement that the\n-global block is writable only through the settings file. It also preserves the\n-accessible-mode stdin hazard and keeps human input inside pre-push execution.\n+This would simplify pre-push, but it would regress an intentional consent flow\n+and force users to leave their push to configure egress. The chosen design keeps\n+the prompt, isolates it from route-selection locks and Git stdin, and fixes the\n+accessible-mode behavior without removing the feature.\n \n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor-design.md\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1787607996549,"completed_at_ms":1787607996618}}
