verified on every read so a short worktree-hash\\ncollision cannot alias another worktree.\\n\\nMutable local activation lives separately in `activation.json`, whose state is\\n`enabled`, `disabled`, or absent. Both files are mode `0600` beneath a\\nuser-owned `0700` Entire runtime directory. Writes use the repository's atomic\\nJSON helper, and malformed or unknown schema versions fail closed. Linked\\nworktrees have independent route and activation records.\\n\\n### Atomic route selection\\n\\nThe first process that needs runtime storage establishes the route before writing\\nruntime data. Read-only commands never call this operation. Competing global-hook\\nand `entire enable` processes use a short, bounded route-selection critical\\nsection:\\n\\n1. derive the deterministic per-worktree marker path;\\n2. acquire the per-worktree route-selection lock only for read/create/publish;\\n3. write and fsync a temporary complete marker, then atomically publish it\\n   without replacing an existing marker;\\n4. on collision, read and use the winner; and\\n5. on an unverifiable result, skip hook capture rather than guessing a route.\\n\\nThe proposal is deterministic for the normal race: while global policy is\\nactive, both a first global hook and concurrent `entire enable` propose the\\ngit-common layout. With global policy inactive, explicit enable proposes the\\nworktree layout. A conflicting proposal caused by a concurrent settings edit is\\nresolved by first published route wins.\\n\\nNo long-held migration lock is needed. Hooks do not block behind interactive\\ninput or condensation, and lock failure cannot fail a Git commit, push, or agent\\nsession.\\n\\nThe existing takeover planner, recursive mover, transcript-path repair,\\nmigration gate, retry marker, and test-only migration wrappers are removed.\\n\\n### Activation and route transitions\\n\\n| Starting state and action | Result |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| No markers, global off | Inactive; read-only commands make no writes |\\n| No markers, global on; first hook | Select git-common route, leave local activation absent, capture globally |\\n| No markers, global off; `entire enable` | Persist repo settings, select worktree route, then atomically set local activation `enabled` |\\n| No markers, global on; `entire enable` | Persist repo settings, select git-common route, then set local activation `enabled` |\\n| Existing route; `entire enable` | Preserve route and set local activation `enabled` |\\n| `entire disable` | Set local activation `disabled`, preserve route and runtime data; this is a per-worktree veto over global activation. A global-only repo writes no worktree file; a locally activated repo also preserves the existing repo-settings disable behavior |\\n| Re-enable after disable | Set local activation `enabled` and reuse the preserved route |\\n| `disable --uninstall` | Remove this worktree's runtime/route data, but retain a minimal `disabled` activation tombstone so always-installed user hooks cannot recreate the integration while global settings remain on. Shared clone Git hooks remain when global policy or another worktree still needs them |\\n| Enable after uninstall | Establish a fresh route from current policy and replace the tombstone with `enabled` |\\n| Legacy enabled, single worktree | Bootstrap only from enabled settings plus a Git-dir Entire hook or verified untracked worktree runtime evidence |\\n| Legacy enabled, linked worktree | Bootstrap only from verified untracked evidence in that exact worktree; otherwise report that `entire enable` must be run once there |\\n| Legacy disabled | Remain inactive; no activation bootstrap |\\n  `content_hash.txt`).\\n\\nEmpty directories, logs, tmp files, project settings, shared/common hooks, and\\nany external or worktree-relative `core.hooksPath` are not bootstrap evidence.\\n\\nA repository-level `enabled: false` may remain an explicit capture veto. An\\n`enabled: true` value configures an already locally or globally activated\\nrepository but does not create activation.\\n\\n### Settings provenance and executable values\\n\\nHook-time settings are exposed through a sanitized view selected by activation\\nsource. Foreground commands unrelated to capture retain their current settings\\nbehavior; this matrix governs agent hooks, Git hooks, checkpoint creation, and\\ncheckpoint egress.\\n\\n| Settings field/group | Global-only activation | Local activation |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| `enabled` | `false` is a capture veto; `true` does not establish activation | Existing merged behavior after the local marker is established |\\n| `log_level` | Allowed | Allowed |\\n| Built-in declarative redaction (`pii`, `custom_redactions`, `externalize_images`) | Allowed; malformed values fail closed | Existing merged behavior |\\n| External scanner/OPF configuration (`openai_privacy_filter`, `betterleaks`, `goredact`) | Ignored; compiled safe defaults only | Existing behavior, including the rule that `opf_command` must come from verified untracked `settings.local.json` |\\n| `strategy_options`, including `checkpoint_remote` | Ignored; default checkpoint strategy and destination derivation | Existing behavior and inherited-remote ownership checks |\\n| `checkpoints`, `sign_checkpoint_commits`, `vercel` | Ignored | Existing behavior |\\n| `absolute_git_hook_path`, `external_agents` | Ignored; global infrastructure uses built-in supported agents only | Existing behavior |\\n| `commit_linking` | Ignored; compiled default | Existing behavior |\\n| Telemetry, review, investigate, and summary-generation settings | Not consumed by the hook-time sanitized view | Unchanged for their existing foreground consumers |\\n\\nThe whitelist is implemented positively; adding a new `EntireSettings` field\\ndoes not automatically make it available to global-only hooks. A test must\\nclassify every new field before the sanitized-view switch can expose it.\\n\\nLocal settings paths are rejected as locally owned if the file or any parent\\npath component traverses a symlink. Tracked, unreadable, malformed, or\\nunverifiable local configuration fails toward the untrusted classification.\\nLocal activation does not relax existing per-field provenance checks: in\\nparticular, a project-file `opf_command` remains rejected after `entire enable`.\\nSymlink validation starts from the canonical worktree root and inspects only the\\nworktree-relative `.entire/settings*.json` components with `lstat`; it does not\\nreject a worktree merely because the caller reached the worktree root through a\\nplatform alias such as macOS `/var` -> `/private/var`.\\n106:\\t// Redaction configures PII redaction behavior for transcripts and metadata.\\n280:type RedactionSettings struct {\\n281:\\tPII *PIISettings `json:\\\"pii,omitempty\\\"`\\n283:\\t// CustomRedactions is a label → RE2 regex map for user-defined patterns\\n288:\\t// \\\"[REDACTED_<LABEL>]\\\" token used by PII. Failed regex compilations are\\n290:\\tCustomRedactions map[string]string `json:\\\"custom_redactions,omitempty\\\"`\\n317:// PIISettings configures PII detection categories.\\n319:type PIISettings struct {\\n1289:\\t\\tif dst.PII == nil {\\n1290:\\t\\t\\tdst.PII = &PIISettings{}\\n1292:\\t\\tif err := mergePIISettings(dst.PII, piiRaw); err != nil {\\n1297:\\t\\tif err := mergeStringMap(&dst.CustomRedactions, csRaw, \\\"redaction.custom_redactions\\\"); err != nil {\\n1397:// mergePIISettings merges PII overrides into existing PIISettings.\\n1400:func mergePIISettings(dst *PIISettings, data json.RawMessage) error {\\n\"}"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a035c5-5c5e-7ca3-86ab-631a16cc0d4a","create_time":1787609029.4943}}}
