{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:07:49.665Z","ordinal":10076,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a035d0-c5a1-7783-a51b-086577b5a434","author":"/root/plan_document_reviewer","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/plan_document_reviewer\nPayload:\n## Plan Review\n**Status:** Issues Found\n**Issues (if any):**\n- [Task 6, Step 3]: The sanitized loader audit covers `settings.Load` but omits hook-reachable `settings.LoadCheckpointsConfig` paths, including `settings/checkpoints.go`, `checkpoint/open.go`, and `strategy/unpushed_checkpoints.go`. - Global-only hooks could still honor repository-supplied checkpoint backend configuration, violating the required default-backend whitelist.\n- [Task 5, Step 5]: Reconciliation does not specify or test the required target filter, bounded per-file locking, or recursion suppression. - The current implementation targets every supported agent and lacks per-file locks, so following this plan could create configs for absent agents or lose concurrent user configuration updates.\n- [Task 3, Steps 5–7]: The uninstall work does not address existing clone-wide cleanup of Git hooks, session states, and shadow branches, nor test uninstall with another active linked worktree. - The spec requires removing only this worktree’s runtime/route data and preserving shared hooks and sibling-worktree state when still needed.\n**Recommendations (advisory, do not block approval):**\n- [Task 2, Step 10]: Stage `settings/hook_settings.go` and its test in the Task 2 commit so the tested provenance boundary is preserved in that slice."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a035c5-5c5e-7ca3-86ab-631a16cc0d4a","create_time":1787609269.66539}}}
