{"timestamp":"2026-08-24T22:35:25.268Z","ordinal":10408,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a025ce-e754-7631-8467-eaa6035ba0f8","turn_id":"01a035c5-5c5e-7ca3-86ab-631a16cc0d4a","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_068dffc2438c6825016a8cc72aad3487d083b664396c98f3aa","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\nThe first task now has one source of truth for strict parsing, normalization, classification, and atomic mutation, while existing callers still see the old `settings` API. That compatibility seam is important: later tasks can replace route and trust internals incrementally without forcing a repository-wide flag day.\n\nThe concurrency guarantee is structural, not just conventional—the flock spans read, mutation, and atomic replacement, and the test exercises competing trust writes.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\nTask 1 is committed locally and fully green. Before moving forward, I’m applying the required two-stage review: first exact requirement compliance, then production-quality review of the commit diff."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1787610922710,"completed_at_ms":1787610925268}}
