{"timestamp":"2026-08-25T00:13:39.583Z","ordinal":11218,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a03643-f97f-7613-a4fa-93db766913a1","call_id":"call_NDRjevgbsFPJnNnp9oUCtv9U","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/efficiency_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Clarity pass complete. The strongest result: `--global` is still fully present, while the merged design retains duplicated settings policy, mixed command scope, and substantial migration/test scaffolding. I sent the prioritized findings and from-scratch recommendations to the parent agent.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/task2_spec_review\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/task2_sticky_routing\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Implemented and committed Task 2.\\n\\nCommit: `c2bfb7681a27f4430b7488f10e3f9d2d2235ec73`  \\nMessage: `refactor(global): make activation and runtime routing sticky`  \\nPush: not performed.\\n\\nRED evidence:\\n\\n- Activation tests failed before `ClassifyRepoPolicy`, activation records, and legacy bootstrap APIs existed.\\n- Provenance tests failed before verified settings provenance, sanitized loading, and exhaustive field classifications existed.\\n- Route tests failed before sticky `EnsureRuntimeRoute` and route records existed.\\n- Additional RED cases caught tracked-local veto, corrupt marker recovery, symlink traversal, and malformed-settings compatibility issues.\\n\\nImplemented:\\n\\n- Versioned per-worktree activation and route records with canonical identity validation.\\n- Atomic `0600` records under `0700` registries.\\n- Explicit disabled veto and explicit-enable-only corrupt activation recovery.\\n- Strict, worktree-specific legacy activation evidence.\\n- First-writer-wins sticky routing with bounded locking and cancellation safety.\\n- Read-only policy classification and context snapshots.\\n- Symlink-safe settings provenance.\\n- Global-only hook settings whitelist with reflection-backed exhaustive classification.\\n- Paths now consume policy routes only for metadata, logs, and tmp.\\n- Linked-worktree, concurrent-writer, cancellation, permissions, symlink, tracked-file, separate-Git-dir, and corrupt-record coverage.\\n- Removed duplicated settings parsing from `paths`.\\n\\nVerification:\\n\\n- Mandated focused suite: passed.\\n- Affected package suites: passed.\\n- `mise run dup`: completed; 920 existing repository-wide advisory matches. The only new changed-code duplication was extracted, leaving changed files clean.\\n- Post-format `mise run lint`: zero issues.\\n- Final corrected-tree `mise run check`: passed completely, including race-enabled unit/integration tests, Vogon canary 56/56, and Roger-Roger 4/4.\\n- `git diff --check`: clean.\\n- Working tree: clean; ignored `docs/superpowers/` remained untouched and uncommitted.\\n\\nThe first full-check attempt exposed 14 lint findings, all resolved. The next run exposed three existing compatibility assertions involving malformed settings and canonical/sticky paths; those were corrected before the final green run.\\n\\nFiles changed: 20 files across `settings/repopolicy`, hook settings, paths, and directly necessary compatibility/test helpers. `paths/worktree.go` needed no edit because Task 1’s shared worktree identity API already satisfied routing.\\n\\nScope note: explicit enable/disable call-site wiring remains assigned to the approved subsequent task; this commit provides the activation APIs and semantics it will consume.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a035c5-5c5e-7ca3-86ab-631a16cc0d4a","create_time":1787616819.583822}}}
