{"timestamp":"2026-08-25T00:15:04.586Z","ordinal":11231,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"agent_message","id":"amsg_01a03645-4589-7c10-a402-c5a8e19a2df4","author":"/root/task2_spec_review","recipient":"/root","content":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Message Type: FINAL_ANSWER\nTask name: /root\nSender: /root/task2_spec_review\nPayload:\nFAIL — 1 commit, 20 files reviewed.\n\n## `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/activation.go`\n\nHigh: Git hooks are accepted as legacy activation evidence at [activation.go:178](</Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/activation.go:178>).\n- Violates: accepted evidence is limited to an exact-worktree live session record or recognized untracked, non-symlinked legacy metadata.\n- Impact: a single-worktree repo with committed `enabled:true` can become locally activated merely because an Entire hook exists, incorrectly pinning runtime data to the worktree.\n- Correction: remove `hasGitDirHookEvidence` from bootstrap and replace the positive test at `activation_test.go:171` with a rejection test.\n\nMedium: “Active session” evidence is not actually validated at [activation.go:285](</Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/activation.go:285>).\n- Any phase except literal `\"ended\"` is accepted, including `\"idle\"`, unknown, or missing. The positive test at `activation_test.go:189` omits `phase` entirely.\n- Impact: stale/idle or malformed session records can bootstrap local activation.\n- Correction: accept only recognized active phases (`active`, and `active_committed` if legacy compatibility requires it), reject idle/unknown/missing, and add positive/negative phase tests.\n\n## `cmd/entire/cli/settings/hook_settings.go`\n\nHigh: PII category pointers are not preserved exactly at [hook_settings.go:189](</Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/cmd/entire/cli/settings/hook_settings.go:189>).\n- A JSON `null` category is unmarshaled into a temporary `bool` and stored as `&false`.\n- Impact: `email:null` or `phone:null` changes the documented default-enabled behavior into disabled, reducing redaction; downstream defaults are applied at `strategy/common.go:504`.\n- Correction: decode category values into `*bool` and preserve nil. Add null-pointer coverage.\n\nMedium: malformed allowed scalar fields do not fail closed at [hook_settings.go:121](</Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/cmd/entire/cli/settings/hook_settings.go:121>) and [hook_settings.go:222](</Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/cmd/entire/cli/settings/hook_settings.go:222>).\n- `encoding/json` accepts `null` into non-pointer booleans/strings without error, so `enabled:null`, `log_level:null`, and `externalize_images:null` pass despite not having the required type.\n- Correction: reject null for non-nullable allowed fields and expand the malformed-field test beyond one string-valued `enabled`.\n\n## `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/route_test.go`\n\nMedium: canceled-waiter coverage is not genuine at [route_test.go:118](</Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/route_test.go:118>).\n- The context is canceled before `EnsureRuntimeRoute` begins, so the function returns at its initial context check; no waiter ever contends on the lock.\n- Correction: hold the route lock, start an `EnsureRuntimeRoute` waiter, cancel while blocked, verify it publishes nothing, release the lock, then verify a live writer wins.\n\n## `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/route.go`\n\nMedium: route publication is not portable to Windows at [route.go:148](</Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/route.go:148>).\n- It propagates directory `Sync` failure after the hard-link publication. The repository’s atomic writer explicitly documents that Windows does not support directory fsync and treats it best-effort.\n- Impact: `EnsureRuntimeRoute` can report failure after successfully publishing the winner on Windows.\n- Correction: use a platform-aware directory-sync helper, preserving strict POSIX sync while tolerating the unsupported Windows operation.\n\n## Duplicate ownership\n\nMedium: the runtime registry layout remains independently owned by both [paths/invisible.go:24](</Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/cmd/entire/cli/paths/invisible.go:24>) and [repopolicy/activation.go:21](</Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/activation.go:21>).\n- Both define and construct `entire/worktree/<key>`, violating the no-duplicate-ownership requirement.\n- Correction: expose one registry-path constructor from `repopolicy` or a cycle-safe leaf and make the paths compatibility facade delegate to it.\n\nFocused verification passed:\n\n`go test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy ./cmd/entire/cli/settings ./cmd/entire/cli/paths -count=1`\n\nThe passing suites do not cover the gaps above."}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a035c5-5c5e-7ca3-86ab-631a16cc0d4a","create_time":1787616904.585991}}}
