{"timestamp":"2026-08-25T00:42:37.975Z","ordinal":11437,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a0365e-8017-7a80-925f-86580936d13e","call_id":"call_eUyDfBtj6zYzP0qy0dPrINrS","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/efficiency_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Clarity pass complete. The strongest result: `--global` is still fully present, while the merged design retains duplicated settings policy, mixed command scope, and substantial migration/test scaffolding. I sent the prioritized findings and from-scratch recommendations to the parent agent.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/task2_quality_review\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/task2_spec_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"PASS — reviewed 2 commits, 25 files across `7bec624c..286ee984`.\\n\\nAll prior findings are fixed:\\n\\n- Hook evidence removed; bootstrap now accepts only session or metadata evidence at `activation.go:176-185`. Negative hook tests cover main and linked worktrees.\\n- Session phases are exact: only `active` and legacy `active_committed` at `activation.go:267-279`; empty, idle, ended, and unknown are rejected by tests.\\n- PII pointer null semantics are preserved at `hook_settings.go:189-198`.\\n- Non-nullable allowed fields reject JSON null at `hook_settings.go:229-234`, with expanded scalar-null tests.\\n- Cancellation now uses a held OS flock and verifies the waiter publishes nothing before a live winner proceeds at `route_test.go:121-163`.\\n- Route directory sync uses platform-specific `jsonutil.SyncDir`; Windows unsupported errors are handled in `syncdir_windows.go`, and `route.go:148-150` uses it.\\n- Runtime registry ownership is centralized in `repopolicy.WorktreeRegistryDir` at `activation.go:24-53`; `paths/invisible.go:30` delegates to it.\\n\\nThe full original requirements also remain satisfied: exact record paths/schema, fail-closed validation, read-only classification, sticky first-writer routing, provenance-sanitized settings, context snapshots, linked/separate-git-dir isolation, permissions, cycle-safe leaf dependencies, and no trust/hook-removal scope creep.\\n\\nVerification passed:\\n\\n- Focused policy concurrency tests, 25 repetitions\\n- Focused concurrency tests under `-race`\\n- `jsonutil`, `repopolicy`, `settings`, and `paths` package suites\\n- Windows/amd64 cross-compilation for `jsonutil` and `repopolicy`\\n- `git diff --check`\\n\\nNo remaining actionable findings.\"}}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a035c5-5c5e-7ca3-86ab-631a16cc0d4a","create_time":1787618557.975752}}}
