{"timestamp":"2026-08-25T00:50:46.001Z","ordinal":11499,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call","id":"fc_068dffc2438c6825016a8ce6e5e01887d09afff47e7784fef6","name":"list_agents","namespace":"collaboration","arguments":"{}","call_id":"call_XZvvhMQgqAMyYiknNqfYZWiH","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a035c5-5c5e-7ca3-86ab-631a16cc0d4a","create_time":1787619043.759136}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-25T00:50:46.066Z","ordinal":11500,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"function_call_output","id":"fco_01a03665-f2b2-7972-a70f-6e280b6a741a","call_id":"call_XZvvhMQgqAMyYiknNqfYZWiH","output":"{\"agents\":[{\"agent_name\":\"/root\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/efficiency_audit\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"Clarity pass complete. The strongest result: `--global` is still fully present, while the merged design retains duplicated settings policy, mixed command scope, and substantial migration/test scaffolding. I sent the prioritized findings and from-scratch recommendations to the parent agent.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/task2_quality_review\",\"agent_status\":{\"completed\":\"### Strengths\\n\\n- Activation and route records are strict-decoded, versioned, canonical-identity-bound, and fail closed on corruption or mismatch.\\n- Route publication correctly combines lock contention handling, no-replace publication, atomic complete JSON, and rereading the winning record.\\n- Global-only settings exclude executable/outbound fields while preserving nullable PII categories.\\n- Focused race tests passed for `repopolicy`, `settings`, `paths`, and `jsonutil`; Windows/amd64 test binaries cross-compiled successfully.\\n\\n### Issues\\n\\n#### Critical\\n\\nNone.\\n\\n#### Important\\n\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/provenance.go:39`, `cmd/entire/cli/settings/hook_settings.go:69`, `cmd/entire/cli/settings/hook_settings.go:113`, `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/activation.go:231` — Settings provenance is checked separately from opening the file. A path component can be replaced with a symlink between `Lstat`/trackedness verification and `ReadFile` or `loadMergedSettings`; the latter anchors `os.OpenRoot` at the already-resolved parent, so swapping `.entire` can redirect it outside the canonical worktree. Fix by opening from an `os.Root` anchored at `repository.WorktreeRoot`, reading the relative settings path through that root, and deriving regular-file/provenance checks from the same opened object.\\n\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/activation.go:148` — `ensureRegistryDir` creates a potentially new directory hierarchy but never syncs the parent directory entries. Syncing `route.json`’s registry directory cannot make a newly created registry path durable in its parent, so a crash can lose the supposedly durable route or activation namespace. Fix by creating missing components individually and syncing each parent after publication, using the platform-aware `jsonutil.SyncDir`.\\n\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/activation.go:304` — Legacy metadata bootstrap can execute one `git ls-files` subprocess per recognized file. A fresh clone containing many tracked `.entire/metadata/<session>/prompt.txt`-style files can impose thousands of subprocesses on every unsuccessful bootstrap attempt. Fix by loading tracked metadata paths once into a set, and preferably bound the filesystem scan by a hook-safe budget.\\n\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/activation_test.go:87`, `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/route_test.go:205` — Permission assertions unconditionally require Unix `0700`/`0600` modes. Go documents that Windows `Chmod` only uses the owner-write bit, so native Windows test execution will fail despite valid behavior. Skip exact mode assertions on Windows or assert platform-appropriate security semantics.\\n\\n#### Minor\\n\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/hook_settings.go:208` — `custom_redactions: null` and `custom_patterns: null` become non-nil empty maps when the destination is nil, unlike normal JSON/full-loader semantics. Fix `mergeHookStringMap` to assign the decoded map wholesale when the destination is nil, preserving nil versus empty.\\n\\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/hook_settings.go:22`, `cmd/entire/cli/settings/hook_settings_test.go:202` — Exhaustiveness covers `EntireSettings` and `RedactionSettings`, but not the manually copied `PIISettings`, and the classification maps do not drive the merge implementation. A future PII field can therefore bypass the explicit classification requirement. Add an exhaustive PII policy and test, ideally making the descriptor used by both validation and copying.\\n\\n### Recommendations\\n\\n- Before integrating hook call sites, ensure the hook boundary classifies once, establishes the route before runtime I/O, and attaches the resulting snapshot with `WithRepoPolicy`; currently no production caller does so.\\n- Add native Windows route-publication tests, since cross-compilation cannot exercise directory syncing, hard-link publication, locking, or Windows mode behavior.\\n- Add adversarial tests that swap `.entire` or a settings file between provenance verification and reading.\\n\\n### Assessment\\n\\nReady to proceed? **With fixes.** The state-machine and locking design is strong, but the provenance TOCTOU gap, incomplete directory durability, pathological bootstrap cost, and Windows test failure should be corrected before treating Task 2 as production-ready.\"}},{\"agent_name\":\"/root/task2_sticky_routing\",\"agent_status\":\"running\"}]}","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a035c5-5c5e-7ca3-86ab-631a16cc0d4a","create_time":1787619046.066047}}}
