{"timestamp":"2026-08-25T01:15:43.288Z","ordinal":11680,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a025ce-e754-7631-8467-eaa6035ba0f8","turn_id":"01a035c5-5c5e-7ca3-86ab-631a16cc0d4a","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_068dffc2438c6825016a8cecbbcfa887d08698a353fa06eb4d","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\nThe provenance boundary now transfers verified content, not a verified pathname. That distinction closes the race: a later path swap cannot change the bytes decoded by the parent settings loader.\n\nLegacy metadata scanning is also bounded in two dimensions—one Git query and a 250 ms filesystem budget—so failed bootstrap cannot turn untrusted repository contents into unbounded hook latency.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\nThe quality fixes are committed and the full gate is green. I’m sending the complete Task 2 range back through the same production reviewer to verify the fixes and catch any regression introduced by the secure-read refactor."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1787620539851,"completed_at_ms":1787620543288}}
