{"timestamp":"2026-08-25T04:44:50.012Z","ordinal":12838,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a025ce-e754-7631-8467-eaa6035ba0f8","turn_id":"01a0371f-4feb-7263-aacd-7041d40b862c","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-cece2df8-d97f-4e1c-9028-d19d9e90ebfd","process_id":"79591","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '514,980p' docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents%20-%20Peyton%E2%80%99s%20MacBook%20Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '514,980p' docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor.md","name":"2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor.md","path":"docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"### Task 4: Preserve and harden trust plus checkpoint egress\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/trust.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/trust_test.go`\n- Modify or delete after facade migration: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/trust.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/trust_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/trust_prompt.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/trust_prompt_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_push.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_sync_remote_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/trust_cmd.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/trust_cmd_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing trust-identity and ledger tests**\n\nCover:\n\n```go\nfunc TestEgressDecision_RequiresEveryFetchAndPushURL(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEgressDecision_UnparseableConfiguredOriginHolds(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEgressDecision_PathAppliesOnlyWhenOriginAbsent(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEgressDecision_GlobalOffDeniesEvenWhenTrustAllIsTrue(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestTrustGrant_OriginPathOriginRemovesOnlyRecordedStaleKeys(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestTrustRevoke_PathOriginPathRemovesEveryRecordedIdentity(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestTrustRevoke_PreservesHandAuthoredUnrelatedEntries(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEgressDecision_CommittedProjectSettingsNeverGrantConsent(t *testing.T)\n```\n\nStore the trust-grant ledger machine-locally under the same per-worktree registry. It records only keys written by CLI/prompt consent so hand-authored settings are not guessed or deleted.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Write failing pre-push behavior tests**\n\nPin all observable outcomes:\n\n```go\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_NoPendingCheckpointDoesNotPrompt(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_YesPersistsRepoTrustRechecksAndDrains(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_NotNowHoldsAndPushContinues(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_AlwaysPersistsTrustAllRechecksAndDrains(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_NonInteractiveHoldsWithoutReadingStdin(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_AccessibleModeNeverImplicitlyGrantsOrPanics(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_PromptOrWriteFailureHoldsWithoutFailingGitPush(t *testing.T)\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Run and verify failures**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'Test(EgressDecision|TrustGrant|TrustRevoke|PrePushTrust)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: FAIL on stale identity cleanup, accessible prompt handling, or the new policy API.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Implement one trust decision tree**\n\n`RepoPolicy.Trust` must carry state and source, not a reusable grant boolean:\n\n```go\ntype TrustDecision struct {\n\tAllowed bool\n\tSource  TrustSource\n\tReason  TrustReason\n\tIdentity TrustIdentity\n}\n```\n\nAfter Yes or Always persists consent, rerun `ClassifyRepoPolicy`; never continue using the pre-write decision. Every other egress entry point consumes the same decision without prompting.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Preserve the three-choice prompt safely**\n\nKeep the existing labels and effects. Read from `/dev/tty` through the repository interactive helper, never Git stdin. In accessible mode require an explicit supported choice; otherwise return held. Abort/error means Not now semantically, logs the operational failure, and does not fail the branch push.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Run focused trust and push tests**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy ./cmd/entire/cli/settings ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'Test(EgressDecision|Trust|Revoke|PrePush|CheckpointSync)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: PASS.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\n\nRun: `mise run check`\n\nCommit:\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy cmd/entire/cli/settings/trust.go cmd/entire/cli/settings/trust_test.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/trust_prompt.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/trust_prompt_test.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_push.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_sync_remote_test.go cmd/entire/cli/trust_cmd.go cmd/entire/cli/trust_cmd_test.go\ngit commit -m \"fix(global): preserve trust while hardening checkpoint egress\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 5: Make Claude and Gemini hook definitions declarative without changing behavior\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/user_hooks.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks_user.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks_user_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks_user.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks_user_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/setup_global.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/setup.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent_group.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent_group_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write contract tests before refactoring implementation**\n\nClaude must retain exactly these eight entries:\n\n```text\nSessionStart\nSessionEnd\nStop\nSubagentStop\nUserPromptSubmit\nPreToolUse[Agent]\nPostToolUse[Agent]\nPostToolUse[TaskCreate|TaskUpdate]\n```\n\nGemini must retain exactly twelve entries:\n\n```text\nSessionStart\nSessionEnd[exit]\nSessionEnd[logout]\nBeforeAgent\nAfterAgent\nBeforeModel\nAfterModel\nBeforeToolSelection\nBeforeTool[*]\nAfterTool[*]\nPreCompress\nNotification\n```\n\nTest both repo and user scopes, current production commands, matchers, unrelated-entry preservation, partial-install repair, legacy Entire-entry replacement, and cross-scope dedup assumptions.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run hook contract tests before changing code**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli -run 'Test.*Hooks' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: existing tests PASS; newly added exact-inventory tests provide the behavior baseline.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Introduce one declarative spec per agent**\n\nUse each agent's existing typed hook model. The spec must drive:\n\n- repo-scope installation;\n- user-scope installation;\n- currentness/completeness checks;\n- recognized Entire-entry removal;\n- expected counts for status/doctor.\n\nDo not create one lossy generic JSON schema across agents. Share orchestration, not agent-specific serialization.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Preserve no-op Gemini events**\n\nDo not remove `AfterModel`, `BeforeToolSelection`, `BeforeTool`, `AfterTool`, or `Notification`, even though their parser currently returns no lifecycle event. Their installed presence and command behavior are part of the product contract.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Reconcile hooks as infrastructure**\n\nUser-hook reconciliation runs only from installer/update integration\n(`curl-bash-post-install`), `entire enable`, `entire agent add`, and confirmed\ndoctor repair. `entire agent remove` removes that agent's user-scope Entire\nentries; repository disable/uninstall does not remove shared user-level\ninfrastructure. Reconciliation does not run inside hooks or read-only commands.\nInstallation errors warn without changing global activation policy.\n\nTarget only agents positively detected as installed or whose existing\nuser-scope configuration already contains an Entire entry; never create an\nabsent agent's config merely because its implementation is registered. Wrap\neach user config's read-modify-write in `flock.AcquireContext` with a named,\nbounded foreground timeout and keep the atomic lossless writer inside that\nlock. Add a concurrent-writer test proving unrelated user edits survive.\n\nAdd recursion suppression at the reconciliation coordinator: reject hook\ncontexts (`currentHookAgentName`/the hook command path) and propagate a private\n`ENTIRE_INTERNAL_USER_HOOK_RECONCILING=1` sentinel to child Entire processes.\nTests must prove a hook invocation and a child invocation make no config writes,\nwhile the four authorized foreground paths do.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Run agent tests and duplication check**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli ./cmd/entire/cli/agent -count=1\nmise run dup\n```\n\nExpected: exact inventory unchanged and repeated install/detect/remove loops eliminated or justified.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\n\nRun: `mise run check`\n\nCommit:\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/agent cmd/entire/cli/agent_group.go cmd/entire/cli/agent_group_test.go cmd/entire/cli/setup.go cmd/entire/cli/setup_global.go\ngit commit -m \"refactor(agents): declare user hook contracts once\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 6: Thread one policy snapshot through hooks and diagnostics\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/root.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/hook_registry.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/hook_registry_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/status.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/status_global_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/doctor.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/doctor_global_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/doctor_logs.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/doctor_bundle.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/config.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/global_warn.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/hook_settings_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/checkpoints.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/checkpoints_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/open.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint_backend_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_remote.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_sync_remote.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_hooks.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_push.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/hooks.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/common.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/unpushed_checkpoints.go`\n- Test: corresponding existing `_test.go` files for each hook-time consumer\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing single-classification tests**\n\nInject a counting classifier and assert one evaluation per process flow:\n\n```go\nfunc TestAgentHook_ClassifiesPolicyOnce(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestGitHook_ClassifiesPolicyOnce(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestStatus_ReadOnlyClassificationCreatesNoFiles(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestDoctor_ReadOnlyScanDoesNotMutatePolicyOrHooksWithoutConfirmation(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestHookPolicyFailureSkipsEntireWithoutFailingHostOperation(t *testing.T)\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run and verify failures**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'Test(AgentHook_ClassifiesPolicyOnce|GitHook_ClassifiesPolicyOnce|Status_ReadOnly|Doctor_ReadOnly|HookPolicyFailure)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: FAIL while consumers independently call settings gates and path probes.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Classify at hook entry and pass the snapshot through context**\n\nFor runtime-writing hooks:\n\n```go\np, err := repopolicy.ClassifyRepoPolicy(ctx)\nif err != nil || !p.Active { return nil }\np, err = repopolicy.EnsureRuntimeRoute(ctx, p)\nif err != nil { logAndSkip(); return nil }\nctx = repopolicy.WithRepoPolicy(ctx, p)\n```\n\nRemove migration-gate acquisition from agent and Git hook entry points. Route failure skips Entire work but not the user's agent, commit, or branch push.\n\nAfter storing the snapshot in context, make `settings.Load(ctx)` delegate to\n`LoadForRepoPolicy` whenever that context contains a policy. Audit every\nhook-reachable `settings.Load` call in `strategy/checkpoint_remote.go`,\n`strategy/checkpoint_sync_remote.go`, `strategy/manual_commit_hooks.go`,\n`strategy/manual_commit_push.go`, `strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go`,\n`strategy/hooks.go`, `strategy/common.go`, and lifecycle/state capture. Add\nconsumer-level tests proving malicious ignored values cannot select an OPF\ncommand, checkpoint remote/backend, external agent, hook path, signing mode, or\ncommit-linking behavior. Foreground commands running without a policy snapshot\nretain the existing full settings behavior.\n\nAudit the parallel checkpoint-config loader too. When context contains a\nglobal-only policy, `settings.LoadCheckpointsConfig` may honor explicit\n`ENTIRE_CHECKPOINTS_*` environment overrides but must not read repository\n`checkpoints` blocks; it returns nil so `checkpoint.Open`,\n`strategy/unpushed_checkpoints.go`, and all push/count paths select the compiled\ndefault backend. Add direct tests in `settings/checkpoints_test.go`, the\ncheckpoint open/backend tests, and the strategy consumer proving a malicious\nproject backend or mirror cannot be constructed. Local activation and\nforeground contexts without a policy retain existing checkpoint configuration.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Convert status and doctor to read-only policy consumers**\n\nStatus reports configured/enabled, settings path, activation source/reason, runtime layout, trust source/held state, and user-hook health. Doctor may repair hooks only on its confirmed repair path; ordinary status/help/auth/version invocations create no activation, route, setup, or agent-config files.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Preserve privacy-critical local failures**\n\nDo not blanket-swallow existing local OPF or redaction failures. Add a regression proving a local OPF safety failure still aborts push while policy/route/setup infrastructure failures do not.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Run focused hook/status/doctor tests**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy -run 'Test(AgentHook|GitHook|Lifecycle|Status|Doctor|HookPolicyFailure|OPF)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: PASS.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\n\nRun: `mise run check`\n\nCommit:\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/root.go cmd/entire/cli/hook_registry.go cmd/entire/cli/hook_registry_test.go cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd.go cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd_test.go cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle_test.go cmd/entire/cli/status.go cmd/entire/cli/status_global_test.go cmd/entire/cli/doctor.go cmd/entire/cli/doctor_global_test.go cmd/entire/cli/doctor_logs.go cmd/entire/cli/doctor_bundle.go cmd/entire/cli/config.go cmd/entire/cli/global_warn.go cmd/entire/cli/settings cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/open.go cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint_backend_test.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy\ngit commit -m \"refactor(global): share one policy snapshot across runtime paths\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 7: Add integration coverage, remove obsolete code, and prepare the coherent PR\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/global_enable_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/checkpoint_sync_remote_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_policy_test.go`\n- Modify: `docs/architecture/agent-integration-checklist.md`\n- Modify: `docs/security-and-privacy.md`\n- Modify: `CLAUDE.md`\n- Delete: obsolete migration-only tests/helpers identified by `rg`\n- Modify: any remaining user-facing source containing removed global-activation guidance\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Replace stacked integration tests with scenario tests**\n\nCreate real-binary integration coverage for:\n\n1. settings-file global activation -> Claude/Gemini user hook -> hidden runtime capture;\n2. no pending checkpoint -> no trust prompt/output;\n3. pending checkpoint -> Yes drains, Not now holds, Always drains all;\n4. non-interactive/accessible prompt paths hold safely without Git stdin reads;\n5. explicit enable after global capture keeps the git-common route;\n6. explicit-first route remains worktree-local after global settings turn on;\n7. fresh clone with committed `enabled: true` gains neither local activation nor egress;\n8. linked worktrees receive independent activation/route records;\n9. tracked or symlinked `.entire` cannot unlock executable settings or egress;\n10. multiple fetch/push URLs require complete trust.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run integration tests and verify failures before final fixes**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\nmise run test:integration\n```\n\nExpected: any remaining wiring gaps fail with a scenario name, not a low-level helper assertion.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Remove obsolete symbols and duplicated tests**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\nrg -n \"runEnableGlobalMode|runDisableGlobalMode|maybePromptGlobalTracking|maybeMigrateGlobalRuntimeData|migration gate|GlobalSetupCompleted|enable --global|disable --global\" --glob '!docs/superpowers/**'\n```\n\nExpected after cleanup: no production symbols or user-facing instructions remain. Historical changelog text may remain only when clearly historical and not presented as current usage.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Audit test quality and duplication**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\nmise run dup\nmise run lint:full\n```\n\nDelete tests that merely repeat implementation details; retain the policy matrix, race tests, security boundaries, exact hook inventories, and real-binary scenarios.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Measure the final diff budget**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngit diff --shortstat origin/main...HEAD\ngit diff --numstat origin/main...HEAD\n```\n\nTarget: approximately 8,000–10,000 additions total, 3,500–4,500 production additions, and materially more deletions than the current stacked branch. If additions remain near 13,000, perform another reuse/test-consolidation pass before landing.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Run final verification**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\nmise run check\nmise run lint\ngit diff --check\n```\n\nExpected: all PASS and worktree contains only intended source/test/doc changes. Do not run paid real-agent E2E tests.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Commit the integration and cleanup slice**\n\n```bash\ngit add CLAUDE.md cmd/entire/cli docs/architecture/agent-integration-checklist.md docs/security-and-privacy.md\ngit commit -m \"test(global): cover settings-only tracking end to end\"\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 8: Review the complete diff against `origin/main`**\n\nUse `entire:review` for intent-aware review, then `superpowers:requesting-code-review`. Address every valid finding and rerun the relevant focused test plus `mise run check` before any fixing commit.\n\n- [ ] **Step 9: Synthesize the clean PR history**\n\nKeep a local backup ref to the implementation branch. Rebuild the final PR head directly on `origin/main` as a coherent commit series or one reviewed squash commit; verify the rebuilt tree is byte-identical to the tested implementation tree before updating PR #2030. Do not preserve the old stack's merge commits or intermediate add-then-remove behavior.\n\n- [ ] **Step 10: Update the remote and close gates**\n\nBefore the authorized remote update, run `mise run lint` again. Update `feat/global-trust` with `--force-with-lease`, update the PR/trail body to describe the single coherent feature, then wait for every repository/PR gate to reach terminal state. Compare pre/post risk and security classifications, inspect every failure/degradation, fix valid findings, and repeat until stable. Resolve trail findings only after their implementation and regression tests are present remotely.\n\n## Finding closure checklist\n\nBefore resolving any trail finding, verify its named regression is present and\npassing:\n\n| Finding | Required regression |\n| --- | --- |\n| `01M0TSFS8WSCD7CNSV5XJ4Q983` migration gate blocks behind prompt/condensation | `TestPrePushTrust_*` plus concurrent route selection prove prompts/condensation run outside route locks |\n| `01M0TSFQ9D1EH7M7VCZ43FYVC6` gate failure aborts host operations | `TestHookPolicyFailureSkipsEntireWithoutFailingHostOperation` covers agent, commit, and branch push; local OPF failure still aborts |\n| `01M0TSEWA8GW6BMQEM98Y5AYMS` committed settings grant egress | `TestEgressDecision_CommittedProjectSettingsNeverGrantConsent` |\n| `01M0TSE2YQG4NHX4HQPK7P7FW6` symlinked `.entire` unlocks executable settings | provenance plus every hook-settings consumer test rejects symlink traversal and ignores executable/outbound fields |\n| `01M0TSDJQKTMR26TPV0Z1N7YG8` accessible prompt grants/panics | `TestPrePushTrust_AccessibleModeNeverImplicitlyGrantsOrPanics` |\n| `01M0TSGCWR0EVVQWK526A4BTEZ` expired try-lock context | barrier-controlled `TestEnsureRuntimeRoute_ConcurrentWritersUseOneCompleteWinner` plus canceled-waiter coverage |\n| `01M0TSEY7XNH32BR7ZXEGEMABS` revoke misses stale identity | both origin→path→origin and path→origin→path grant-ledger/revoke tests |\n| `01M0TSGEJB4B513AV3TS310RN0` disabled tier conflicts with `trust_all` | `TestEgressDecision_GlobalOffDeniesEvenWhenTrustAllIsTrue` |\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"### Task 4: Preserve and harden trust plus checkpoint egress\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/trust.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/trust_test.go`\n- Modify or delete after facade migration: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/trust.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/trust_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/trust_prompt.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/trust_prompt_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_push.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_sync_remote_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/trust_cmd.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/trust_cmd_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing trust-identity and ledger tests**\n\nCover:\n\n```go\nfunc TestEgressDecision_RequiresEveryFetchAndPushURL(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEgressDecision_UnparseableConfiguredOriginHolds(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEgressDecision_PathAppliesOnlyWhenOriginAbsent(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEgressDecision_GlobalOffDeniesEvenWhenTrustAllIsTrue(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestTrustGrant_OriginPathOriginRemovesOnlyRecordedStaleKeys(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestTrustRevoke_PathOriginPathRemovesEveryRecordedIdentity(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestTrustRevoke_PreservesHandAuthoredUnrelatedEntries(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEgressDecision_CommittedProjectSettingsNeverGrantConsent(t *testing.T)\n```\n\nStore the trust-grant ledger machine-locally under the same per-worktree registry. It records only keys written by CLI/prompt consent so hand-authored settings are not guessed or deleted.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Write failing pre-push behavior tests**\n\nPin all observable outcomes:\n\n```go\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_NoPendingCheckpointDoesNotPrompt(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_YesPersistsRepoTrustRechecksAndDrains(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_NotNowHoldsAndPushContinues(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_AlwaysPersistsTrustAllRechecksAndDrains(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_NonInteractiveHoldsWithoutReadingStdin(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_AccessibleModeNeverImplicitlyGrantsOrPanics(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_PromptOrWriteFailureHoldsWithoutFailingGitPush(t *testing.T)\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Run and verify failures**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'Test(EgressDecision|TrustGrant|TrustRevoke|PrePushTrust)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: FAIL on stale identity cleanup, accessible prompt handling, or the new policy API.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Implement one trust decision tree**\n\n`RepoPolicy.Trust` must carry state and source, not a reusable grant boolean:\n\n```go\ntype TrustDecision struct {\n\tAllowed bool\n\tSource  TrustSource\n\tReason  TrustReason\n\tIdentity TrustIdentity\n}\n```\n\nAfter Yes or Always persists consent, rerun `ClassifyRepoPolicy`; never continue using the pre-write decision. Every other egress entry point consumes the same decision without prompting.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Preserve the three-choice prompt safely**\n\nKeep the existing labels and effects. Read from `/dev/tty` through the repository interactive helper, never Git stdin. In accessible mode require an explicit supported choice; otherwise return held. Abort/error means Not now semantically, logs the operational failure, and does not fail the branch push.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Run focused trust and push tests**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy ./cmd/entire/cli/settings ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'Test(EgressDecision|Trust|Revoke|PrePush|CheckpointSync)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: PASS.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\n\nRun: `mise run check`\n\nCommit:\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy cmd/entire/cli/settings/trust.go cmd/entire/cli/settings/trust_test.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/trust_prompt.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/trust_prompt_test.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_push.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_sync_remote_test.go cmd/entire/cli/trust_cmd.go cmd/entire/cli/trust_cmd_test.go\ngit commit -m \"fix(global): preserve trust while hardening checkpoint egress\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 5: Make Claude and Gemini hook definitions declarative without changing behavior\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/user_hooks.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks_user.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks_user_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks_user.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks_user_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/setup_global.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/setup.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent_group.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent_group_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write contract tests before refactoring implementation**\n\nClaude must retain exactly these eight entries:\n\n```text\nSessionStart\nSessionEnd\nStop\nSubagentStop\nUserPromptSubmit\nPreToolUse[Agent]\nPostToolUse[Agent]\nPostToolUse[TaskCreate|TaskUpdate]\n```\n\nGemini must retain exactly twelve entries:\n\n```text\nSessionStart\nSessionEnd[exit]\nSessionEnd[logout]\nBeforeAgent\nAfterAgent\nBeforeModel\nAfterModel\nBeforeToolSelection\nBeforeTool[*]\nAfterTool[*]\nPreCompress\nNotification\n```\n\nTest both repo and user scopes, current production commands, matchers, unrelated-entry preservation, partial-install repair, legacy Entire-entry replacement, and cross-scope dedup assumptions.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run hook contract tests before changing code**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli -run 'Test.*Hooks' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: existing tests PASS; newly added exact-inventory tests provide the behavior baseline.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Introduce one declarative spec per agent**\n\nUse each agent's existing typed hook model. The spec must drive:\n\n- repo-scope installation;\n- user-scope installation;\n- currentness/completeness checks;\n- recognized Entire-entry removal;\n- expected counts for status/doctor.\n\nDo not create one lossy generic JSON schema across agents. Share orchestration, not agent-specific serialization.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Preserve no-op Gemini events**\n\nDo not remove `AfterModel`, `BeforeToolSelection`, `BeforeTool`, `AfterTool`, or `Notification`, even though their parser currently returns no lifecycle event. Their installed presence and command behavior are part of the product contract.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Reconcile hooks as infrastructure**\n\nUser-hook reconciliation runs only from installer/update integration\n(`curl-bash-post-install`), `entire enable`, `entire agent add`, and confirmed\ndoctor repair. `entire agent remove` removes that agent's user-scope Entire\nentries; repository disable/uninstall does not remove shared user-level\ninfrastructure. Reconciliation does not run inside hooks or read-only commands.\nInstallation errors warn without changing global activation policy.\n\nTarget only agents positively detected as installed or whose existing\nuser-scope configuration already contains an Entire entry; never create an\nabsent agent's config merely because its implementation is registered. Wrap\neach user config's read-modify-write in `flock.AcquireContext` with a named,\nbounded foreground timeout and keep the atomic lossless writer inside that\nlock. Add a concurrent-writer test proving unrelated user edits survive.\n\nAdd recursion suppression at the reconciliation coordinator: reject hook\ncontexts (`currentHookAgentName`/the hook command path) and propagate a private\n`ENTIRE_INTERNAL_USER_HOOK_RECONCILING=1` sentinel to child Entire processes.\nTests must prove a hook invocation and a child invocation make no config writes,\nwhile the four authorized foreground paths do.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Run agent tests and duplication check**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli ./cmd/entire/cli/agent -count=1\nmise run dup\n```\n\nExpected: exact inventory unchanged and repeated install/detect/remove loops eliminated or justified.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\n\nRun: `mise run check`\n\nCommit:\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/agent cmd/entire/cli/agent_group.go cmd/entire/cli/agent_group_test.go cmd/entire/cli/setup.go cmd/entire/cli/setup_global.go\ngit commit -m \"refactor(agents): declare user hook contracts once\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 6: Thread one policy snapshot through hooks and diagnostics\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/root.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/hook_registry.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/hook_registry_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/status.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/status_global_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/doctor.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/doctor_global_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/doctor_logs.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/doctor_bundle.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/config.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/global_warn.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/hook_settings_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/checkpoints.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/checkpoints_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/open.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint_backend_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_remote.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_sync_remote.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_hooks.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_push.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/hooks.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/common.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/unpushed_checkpoints.go`\n- Test: corresponding existing `_test.go` files for each hook-time consumer\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing single-classification tests**\n\nInject a counting classifier and assert one evaluation per process flow:\n\n```go\nfunc TestAgentHook_ClassifiesPolicyOnce(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestGitHook_ClassifiesPolicyOnce(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestStatus_ReadOnlyClassificationCreatesNoFiles(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestDoctor_ReadOnlyScanDoesNotMutatePolicyOrHooksWithoutConfirmation(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestHookPolicyFailureSkipsEntireWithoutFailingHostOperation(t *testing.T)\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run and verify failures**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'Test(AgentHook_ClassifiesPolicyOnce|GitHook_ClassifiesPolicyOnce|Status_ReadOnly|Doctor_ReadOnly|HookPolicyFailure)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: FAIL while consumers independently call settings gates and path probes.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Classify at hook entry and pass the snapshot through context**\n\nFor runtime-writing hooks:\n\n```go\np, err := repopolicy.ClassifyRepoPolicy(ctx)\nif err != nil || !p.Active { return nil }\np, err = repopolicy.EnsureRuntimeRoute(ctx, p)\nif err != nil { logAndSkip(); return nil }\nctx = repopolicy.WithRepoPolicy(ctx, p)\n```\n\nRemove migration-gate acquisition from agent and Git hook entry points. Route failure skips Entire work but not the user's agent, commit, or branch push.\n\nAfter storing the snapshot in context, make `settings.Load(ctx)` delegate to\n`LoadForRepoPolicy` whenever that context contains a policy. Audit every\nhook-reachable `settings.Load` call in `strategy/checkpoint_remote.go`,\n`strategy/checkpoint_sync_remote.go`, `strategy/manual_commit_hooks.go`,\n`strategy/manual_commit_push.go`, `strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go`,\n`strategy/hooks.go`, `strategy/common.go`, and lifecycle/state capture. Add\nconsumer-level tests proving malicious ignored values cannot select an OPF\ncommand, checkpoint remote/backend, external agent, hook path, signing mode, or\ncommit-linking behavior. Foreground commands running without a policy snapshot\nretain the existing full settings behavior.\n\nAudit the parallel checkpoint-config loader too. When context contains a\nglobal-only policy, `settings.LoadCheckpointsConfig` may honor explicit\n`ENTIRE_CHECKPOINTS_*` environment overrides but must not read repository\n`checkpoints` blocks; it returns nil so `checkpoint.Open`,\n`strategy/unpushed_checkpoints.go`, and all push/count paths select the compiled\ndefault backend. Add direct tests in `settings/checkpoints_test.go`, the\ncheckpoint open/backend tests, and the strategy consumer proving a malicious\nproject backend or mirror cannot be constructed. Local activation and\nforeground contexts without a policy retain existing checkpoint configuration.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Convert status and doctor to read-only policy consumers**\n\nStatus reports configured/enabled, settings path, activation source/reason, runtime layout, trust source/held state, and user-hook health. Doctor may repair hooks only on its confirmed repair path; ordinary status/help/auth/version invocations create no activation, route, setup, or agent-config files.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Preserve privacy-critical local failures**\n\nDo not blanket-swallow existing local OPF or redaction failures. Add a regression proving a local OPF safety failure still aborts push while policy/route/setup infrastructure failures do not.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Run focused hook/status/doctor tests**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy -run 'Test(AgentHook|GitHook|Lifecycle|Status|Doctor|HookPolicyFailure|OPF)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: PASS.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\n\nRun: `mise run check`\n\nCommit:\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/root.go cmd/entire/cli/hook_registry.go cmd/entire/cli/hook_registry_test.go cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd.go cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd_test.go cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle_test.go cmd/entire/cli/status.go cmd/entire/cli/status_global_test.go cmd/entire/cli/doctor.go cmd/entire/cli/doctor_global_test.go cmd/entire/cli/doctor_logs.go cmd/entire/cli/doctor_bundle.go cmd/entire/cli/config.go cmd/entire/cli/global_warn.go cmd/entire/cli/settings cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/open.go cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint_backend_test.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy\ngit commit -m \"refactor(global): share one policy snapshot across runtime paths\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 7: Add integration coverage, remove obsolete code, and prepare the coherent PR\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/global_enable_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/checkpoint_sync_remote_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_policy_test.go`\n- Modify: `docs/architecture/agent-integration-checklist.md`\n- Modify: `docs/security-and-privacy.md`\n- Modify: `CLAUDE.md`\n- Delete: obsolete migration-only tests/helpers identified by `rg`\n- Modify: any remaining user-facing source containing removed global-activation guidance\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Replace stacked integration tests with scenario tests**\n\nCreate real-binary integration coverage for:\n\n1. settings-file global activation -> Claude/Gemini user hook -> hidden runtime capture;\n2. no pending checkpoint -> no trust prompt/output;\n3. pending checkpoint -> Yes drains, Not now holds, Always drains all;\n4. non-interactive/accessible prompt paths hold safely without Git stdin reads;\n5. explicit enable after global capture keeps the git-common route;\n6. explicit-first route remains worktree-local after global settings turn on;\n7. fresh clone with committed `enabled: true` gains neither local activation nor egress;\n8. linked worktrees receive independent activation/route records;\n9. tracked or symlinked `.entire` cannot unlock executable settings or egress;\n10. multiple fetch/push URLs require complete trust.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run integration tests and verify failures before final fixes**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\nmise run test:integration\n```\n\nExpected: any remaining wiring gaps fail with a scenario name, not a low-level helper assertion.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Remove obsolete symbols and duplicated tests**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\nrg -n \"runEnableGlobalMode|runDisableGlobalMode|maybePromptGlobalTracking|maybeMigrateGlobalRuntimeData|migration gate|GlobalSetupCompleted|enable --global|disable --global\" --glob '!docs/superpowers/**'\n```\n\nExpected after cleanup: no production symbols or user-facing instructions remain. Historical changelog text may remain only when clearly historical and not presented as current usage.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Audit test quality and duplication**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\nmise run dup\nmise run lint:full\n```\n\nDelete tests that merely repeat implementation details; retain the policy matrix, race tests, security boundaries, exact hook inventories, and real-binary scenarios.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Measure the final diff budget**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngit diff --shortstat origin/main...HEAD\ngit diff --numstat origin/main...HEAD\n```\n\nTarget: approximately 8,000–10,000 additions total, 3,500–4,500 production additions, and materially more deletions than the current stacked branch. If additions remain near 13,000, perform another reuse/test-consolidation pass before landing.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Run final verification**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\nmise run check\nmise run lint\ngit diff --check\n```\n\nExpected: all PASS and worktree contains only intended source/test/doc changes. Do not run paid real-agent E2E tests.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Commit the integration and cleanup slice**\n\n```bash\ngit add CLAUDE.md cmd/entire/cli docs/architecture/agent-integration-checklist.md docs/security-and-privacy.md\ngit commit -m \"test(global): cover settings-only tracking end to end\"\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 8: Review the complete diff against `origin/main`**\n\nUse `entire:review` for intent-aware review, then `superpowers:requesting-code-review`. Address every valid finding and rerun the relevant focused test plus `mise run check` before any fixing commit.\n\n- [ ] **Step 9: Synthesize the clean PR history**\n\nKeep a local backup ref to the implementation branch. Rebuild the final PR head directly on `origin/main` as a coherent commit series or one reviewed squash commit; verify the rebuilt tree is byte-identical to the tested implementation tree before updating PR #2030. Do not preserve the old stack's merge commits or intermediate add-then-remove behavior.\n\n- [ ] **Step 10: Update the remote and close gates**\n\nBefore the authorized remote update, run `mise run lint` again. Update `feat/global-trust` with `--force-with-lease`, update the PR/trail body to describe the single coherent feature, then wait for every repository/PR gate to reach terminal state. Compare pre/post risk and security classifications, inspect every failure/degradation, fix valid findings, and repeat until stable. Resolve trail findings only after their implementation and regression tests are present remotely.\n\n## Finding closure checklist\n\nBefore resolving any trail finding, verify its named regression is present and\npassing:\n\n| Finding | Required regression |\n| --- | --- |\n| `01M0TSFS8WSCD7CNSV5XJ4Q983` migration gate blocks behind prompt/condensation | `TestPrePushTrust_*` plus concurrent route selection prove prompts/condensation run outside route locks |\n| `01M0TSFQ9D1EH7M7VCZ43FYVC6` gate failure aborts host operations | `TestHookPolicyFailureSkipsEntireWithoutFailingHostOperation` covers agent, commit, and branch push; local OPF failure still aborts |\n| `01M0TSEWA8GW6BMQEM98Y5AYMS` committed settings grant egress | `TestEgressDecision_CommittedProjectSettingsNeverGrantConsent` |\n| `01M0TSE2YQG4NHX4HQPK7P7FW6` symlinked `.entire` unlocks executable settings | provenance plus every hook-settings consumer test rejects symlink traversal and ignores executable/outbound fields |\n| `01M0TSDJQKTMR26TPV0Z1N7YG8` accessible prompt grants/panics | `TestPrePushTrust_AccessibleModeNeverImplicitlyGrantsOrPanics` |\n| `01M0TSGCWR0EVVQWK526A4BTEZ` expired try-lock context | barrier-controlled `TestEnsureRuntimeRoute_ConcurrentWritersUseOneCompleteWinner` plus canceled-waiter coverage |\n| `01M0TSEY7XNH32BR7ZXEGEMABS` revoke misses stale identity | both origin→path→origin and path→origin→path grant-ledger/revoke tests |\n| `01M0TSGEJB4B513AV3TS310RN0` disabled tier conflicts with `trust_all` | `TestEgressDecision_GlobalOffDeniesEvenWhenTrustAllIsTrue` |\n","exit_code":0,"duration":{"secs":0,"nanos":7417},"formatted_output":"### Task 4: Preserve and harden trust plus checkpoint egress\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/trust.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/trust_test.go`\n- Modify or delete after facade migration: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/trust.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/trust_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/trust_prompt.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/trust_prompt_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_push.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_sync_remote_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/trust_cmd.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/trust_cmd_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing trust-identity and ledger tests**\n\nCover:\n\n```go\nfunc TestEgressDecision_RequiresEveryFetchAndPushURL(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEgressDecision_UnparseableConfiguredOriginHolds(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEgressDecision_PathAppliesOnlyWhenOriginAbsent(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEgressDecision_GlobalOffDeniesEvenWhenTrustAllIsTrue(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestTrustGrant_OriginPathOriginRemovesOnlyRecordedStaleKeys(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestTrustRevoke_PathOriginPathRemovesEveryRecordedIdentity(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestTrustRevoke_PreservesHandAuthoredUnrelatedEntries(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEgressDecision_CommittedProjectSettingsNeverGrantConsent(t *testing.T)\n```\n\nStore the trust-grant ledger machine-locally under the same per-worktree registry. It records only keys written by CLI/prompt consent so hand-authored settings are not guessed or deleted.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Write failing pre-push behavior tests**\n\nPin all observable outcomes:\n\n```go\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_NoPendingCheckpointDoesNotPrompt(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_YesPersistsRepoTrustRechecksAndDrains(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_NotNowHoldsAndPushContinues(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_AlwaysPersistsTrustAllRechecksAndDrains(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_NonInteractiveHoldsWithoutReadingStdin(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_AccessibleModeNeverImplicitlyGrantsOrPanics(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_PromptOrWriteFailureHoldsWithoutFailingGitPush(t *testing.T)\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Run and verify failures**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'Test(EgressDecision|TrustGrant|TrustRevoke|PrePushTrust)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: FAIL on stale identity cleanup, accessible prompt handling, or the new policy API.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Implement one trust decision tree**\n\n`RepoPolicy.Trust` must carry state and source, not a reusable grant boolean:\n\n```go\ntype TrustDecision struct {\n\tAllowed bool\n\tSource  TrustSource\n\tReason  TrustReason\n\tIdentity TrustIdentity\n}\n```\n\nAfter Yes or Always persists consent, rerun `ClassifyRepoPolicy`; never continue using the pre-write decision. Every other egress entry point consumes the same decision without prompting.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Preserve the three-choice prompt safely**\n\nKeep the existing labels and effects. Read from `/dev/tty` through the repository interactive helper, never Git stdin. In accessible mode require an explicit supported choice; otherwise return held. Abort/error means Not now semantically, logs the operational failure, and does not fail the branch push.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Run focused trust and push tests**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy ./cmd/entire/cli/settings ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'Test(EgressDecision|Trust|Revoke|PrePush|CheckpointSync)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: PASS.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\n\nRun: `mise run check`\n\nCommit:\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy cmd/entire/cli/settings/trust.go cmd/entire/cli/settings/trust_test.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/trust_prompt.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/trust_prompt_test.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_push.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_sync_remote_test.go cmd/entire/cli/trust_cmd.go cmd/entire/cli/trust_cmd_test.go\ngit commit -m \"fix(global): preserve trust while hardening checkpoint egress\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 5: Make Claude and Gemini hook definitions declarative without changing behavior\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/user_hooks.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks_user.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks_user_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks_user.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks_user_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/setup_global.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/setup.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent_group.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent_group_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write contract tests before refactoring implementation**\n\nClaude must retain exactly these eight entries:\n\n```text\nSessionStart\nSessionEnd\nStop\nSubagentStop\nUserPromptSubmit\nPreToolUse[Agent]\nPostToolUse[Agent]\nPostToolUse[TaskCreate|TaskUpdate]\n```\n\nGemini must retain exactly twelve entries:\n\n```text\nSessionStart\nSessionEnd[exit]\nSessionEnd[logout]\nBeforeAgent\nAfterAgent\nBeforeModel\nAfterModel\nBeforeToolSelection\nBeforeTool[*]\nAfterTool[*]\nPreCompress\nNotification\n```\n\nTest both repo and user scopes, current production commands, matchers, unrelated-entry preservation, partial-install repair, legacy Entire-entry replacement, and cross-scope dedup assumptions.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run hook contract tests before changing code**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli -run 'Test.*Hooks' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: existing tests PASS; newly added exact-inventory tests provide the behavior baseline.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Introduce one declarative spec per agent**\n\nUse each agent's existing typed hook model. The spec must drive:\n\n- repo-scope installation;\n- user-scope installation;\n- currentness/completeness checks;\n- recognized Entire-entry removal;\n- expected counts for status/doctor.\n\nDo not create one lossy generic JSON schema across agents. Share orchestration, not agent-specific serialization.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Preserve no-op Gemini events**\n\nDo not remove `AfterModel`, `BeforeToolSelection`, `BeforeTool`, `AfterTool`, or `Notification`, even though their parser currently returns no lifecycle event. Their installed presence and command behavior are part of the product contract.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Reconcile hooks as infrastructure**\n\nUser-hook reconciliation runs only from installer/update integration\n(`curl-bash-post-install`), `entire enable`, `entire agent add`, and confirmed\ndoctor repair. `entire agent remove` removes that agent's user-scope Entire\nentries; repository disable/uninstall does not remove shared user-level\ninfrastructure. Reconciliation does not run inside hooks or read-only commands.\nInstallation errors warn without changing global activation policy.\n\nTarget only agents positively detected as installed or whose existing\nuser-scope configuration already contains an Entire entry; never create an\nabsent agent's config merely because its implementation is registered. Wrap\neach user config's read-modify-write in `flock.AcquireContext` with a named,\nbounded foreground timeout and keep the atomic lossless writer inside that\nlock. Add a concurrent-writer test proving unrelated user edits survive.\n\nAdd recursion suppression at the reconciliation coordinator: reject hook\ncontexts (`currentHookAgentName`/the hook command path) and propagate a private\n`ENTIRE_INTERNAL_USER_HOOK_RECONCILING=1` sentinel to child Entire processes.\nTests must prove a hook invocation and a child invocation make no config writes,\nwhile the four authorized foreground paths do.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Run agent tests and duplication check**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli ./cmd/entire/cli/agent -count=1\nmise run dup\n```\n\nExpected: exact inventory unchanged and repeated install/detect/remove loops eliminated or justified.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\n\nRun: `mise run check`\n\nCommit:\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/agent cmd/entire/cli/agent_group.go cmd/entire/cli/agent_group_test.go cmd/entire/cli/setup.go cmd/entire/cli/setup_global.go\ngit commit -m \"refactor(agents): declare user hook contracts once\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 6: Thread one policy snapshot through hooks and diagnostics\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/root.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/hook_registry.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/hook_registry_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/status.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/status_global_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/doctor.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/doctor_global_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/doctor_logs.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/doctor_bundle.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/config.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/global_warn.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/hook_settings_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/checkpoints.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/checkpoints_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/open.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint_backend_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_remote.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_sync_remote.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_hooks.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_push.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/hooks.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/common.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/unpushed_checkpoints.go`\n- Test: corresponding existing `_test.go` files for each hook-time consumer\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing single-classification tests**\n\nInject a counting classifier and assert one evaluation per process flow:\n\n```go\nfunc TestAgentHook_ClassifiesPolicyOnce(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestGitHook_ClassifiesPolicyOnce(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestStatus_ReadOnlyClassificationCreatesNoFiles(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestDoctor_ReadOnlyScanDoesNotMutatePolicyOrHooksWithoutConfirmation(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestHookPolicyFailureSkipsEntireWithoutFailingHostOperation(t *testing.T)\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run and verify failures**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'Test(AgentHook_ClassifiesPolicyOnce|GitHook_ClassifiesPolicyOnce|Status_ReadOnly|Doctor_ReadOnly|HookPolicyFailure)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: FAIL while consumers independently call settings gates and path probes.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Classify at hook entry and pass the snapshot through context**\n\nFor runtime-writing hooks:\n\n```go\np, err := repopolicy.ClassifyRepoPolicy(ctx)\nif err != nil || !p.Active { return nil }\np, err = repopolicy.EnsureRuntimeRoute(ctx, p)\nif err != nil { logAndSkip(); return nil }\nctx = repopolicy.WithRepoPolicy(ctx, p)\n```\n\nRemove migration-gate acquisition from agent and Git hook entry points. Route failure skips Entire work but not the user's agent, commit, or branch push.\n\nAfter storing the snapshot in context, make `settings.Load(ctx)` delegate to\n`LoadForRepoPolicy` whenever that context contains a policy. Audit every\nhook-reachable `settings.Load` call in `strategy/checkpoint_remote.go`,\n`strategy/checkpoint_sync_remote.go`, `strategy/manual_commit_hooks.go`,\n`strategy/manual_commit_push.go`, `strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go`,\n`strategy/hooks.go`, `strategy/common.go`, and lifecycle/state capture. Add\nconsumer-level tests proving malicious ignored values cannot select an OPF\ncommand, checkpoint remote/backend, external agent, hook path, signing mode, or\ncommit-linking behavior. Foreground commands running without a policy snapshot\nretain the existing full settings behavior.\n\nAudit the parallel checkpoint-config loader too. When context contains a\nglobal-only policy, `settings.LoadCheckpointsConfig` may honor explicit\n`ENTIRE_CHECKPOINTS_*` environment overrides but must not read repository\n`checkpoints` blocks; it returns nil so `checkpoint.Open`,\n`strategy/unpushed_checkpoints.go`, and all push/count paths select the compiled\ndefault backend. Add direct tests in `settings/checkpoints_test.go`, the\ncheckpoint open/backend tests, and the strategy consumer proving a malicious\nproject backend or mirror cannot be constructed. Local activation and\nforeground contexts without a policy retain existing checkpoint configuration.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Convert status and doctor to read-only policy consumers**\n\nStatus reports configured/enabled, settings path, activation source/reason, runtime layout, trust source/held state, and user-hook health. Doctor may repair hooks only on its confirmed repair path; ordinary status/help/auth/version invocations create no activation, route, setup, or agent-config files.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Preserve privacy-critical local failures**\n\nDo not blanket-swallow existing local OPF or redaction failures. Add a regression proving a local OPF safety failure still aborts push while policy/route/setup infrastructure failures do not.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Run focused hook/status/doctor tests**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy -run 'Test(AgentHook|GitHook|Lifecycle|Status|Doctor|HookPolicyFailure|OPF)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: PASS.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\n\nRun: `mise run check`\n\nCommit:\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/root.go cmd/entire/cli/hook_registry.go cmd/entire/cli/hook_registry_test.go cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd.go cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd_test.go cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle_test.go cmd/entire/cli/status.go cmd/entire/cli/status_global_test.go cmd/entire/cli/doctor.go cmd/entire/cli/doctor_global_test.go cmd/entire/cli/doctor_logs.go cmd/entire/cli/doctor_bundle.go cmd/entire/cli/config.go cmd/entire/cli/global_warn.go cmd/entire/cli/settings cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/open.go cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint_backend_test.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy\ngit commit -m \"refactor(global): share one policy snapshot across runtime paths\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 7: Add integration coverage, remove obsolete code, and prepare the coherent PR\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/global_enable_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/checkpoint_sync_remote_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_policy_test.go`\n- Modify: `docs/architecture/agent-integration-checklist.md`\n- Modify: `docs/security-and-privacy.md`\n- Modify: `CLAUDE.md`\n- Delete: obsolete migration-only tests/helpers identified by `rg`\n- Modify: any remaining user-facing source containing removed global-activation guidance\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Replace stacked integration tests with scenario tests**\n\nCreate real-binary integration coverage for:\n\n1. settings-file global activation -> Claude/Gemini user hook -> hidden runtime capture;\n2. no pending checkpoint -> no trust prompt/output;\n3. pending checkpoint -> Yes drains, Not now holds, Always drains all;\n4. non-interactive/accessible prompt paths hold safely without Git stdin reads;\n5. explicit enable after global capture keeps the git-common route;\n6. explicit-first route remains worktree-local after global settings turn on;\n7. fresh clone with committed `enabled: true` gains neither local activation nor egress;\n8. linked worktrees receive independent activation/route records;\n9. tracked or symlinked `.entire` cannot unlock executable settings or egress;\n10. multiple fetch/push URLs require complete trust.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run integration tests and verify failures before final fixes**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\nmise run test:integration\n```\n\nExpected: any remaining wiring gaps fail with a scenario name, not a low-level helper assertion.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Remove obsolete symbols and duplicated tests**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\nrg -n \"runEnableGlobalMode|runDisableGlobalMode|maybePromptGlobalTracking|maybeMigrateGlobalRuntimeData|migration gate|GlobalSetupCompleted|enable --global|disable --global\" --glob '!docs/superpowers/**'\n```\n\nExpected after cleanup: no production symbols or user-facing instructions remain. Historical changelog text may remain only when clearly historical and not presented as current usage.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Audit test quality and duplication**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\nmise run dup\nmise run lint:full\n```\n\nDelete tests that merely repeat implementation details; retain the policy matrix, race tests, security boundaries, exact hook inventories, and real-binary scenarios.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Measure the final diff budget**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngit diff --shortstat origin/main...HEAD\ngit diff --numstat origin/main...HEAD\n```\n\nTarget: approximately 8,000–10,000 additions total, 3,500–4,500 production additions, and materially more deletions than the current stacked branch. If additions remain near 13,000, perform another reuse/test-consolidation pass before landing.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Run final verification**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\nmise run check\nmise run lint\ngit diff --check\n```\n\nExpected: all PASS and worktree contains only intended source/test/doc changes. Do not run paid real-agent E2E tests.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Commit the integration and cleanup slice**\n\n```bash\ngit add CLAUDE.md cmd/entire/cli docs/architecture/agent-integration-checklist.md docs/security-and-privacy.md\ngit commit -m \"test(global): cover settings-only tracking end to end\"\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 8: Review the complete diff against `origin/main`**\n\nUse `entire:review` for intent-aware review, then `superpowers:requesting-code-review`. Address every valid finding and rerun the relevant focused test plus `mise run check` before any fixing commit.\n\n- [ ] **Step 9: Synthesize the clean PR history**\n\nKeep a local backup ref to the implementation branch. Rebuild the final PR head directly on `origin/main` as a coherent commit series or one reviewed squash commit; verify the rebuilt tree is byte-identical to the tested implementation tree before updating PR #2030. Do not preserve the old stack's merge commits or intermediate add-then-remove behavior.\n\n- [ ] **Step 10: Update the remote and close gates**\n\nBefore the authorized remote update, run `mise run lint` again. Update `feat/global-trust` with `--force-with-lease`, update the PR/trail body to describe the single coherent feature, then wait for every repository/PR gate to reach terminal state. Compare pre/post risk and security classifications, inspect every failure/degradation, fix valid findings, and repeat until stable. Resolve trail findings only after their implementation and regression tests are present remotely.\n\n## Finding closure checklist\n\nBefore resolving any trail finding, verify its named regression is present and\npassing:\n\n| Finding | Required regression |\n| --- | --- |\n| `01M0TSFS8WSCD7CNSV5XJ4Q983` migration gate blocks behind prompt/condensation | `TestPrePushTrust_*` plus concurrent route selection prove prompts/condensation run outside route locks |\n| `01M0TSFQ9D1EH7M7VCZ43FYVC6` gate failure aborts host operations | `TestHookPolicyFailureSkipsEntireWithoutFailingHostOperation` covers agent, commit, and branch push; local OPF failure still aborts |\n| `01M0TSEWA8GW6BMQEM98Y5AYMS` committed settings grant egress | `TestEgressDecision_CommittedProjectSettingsNeverGrantConsent` |\n| `01M0TSE2YQG4NHX4HQPK7P7FW6` symlinked `.entire` unlocks executable settings | provenance plus every hook-settings consumer test rejects symlink traversal and ignores executable/outbound fields |\n| `01M0TSDJQKTMR26TPV0Z1N7YG8` accessible prompt grants/panics | `TestPrePushTrust_AccessibleModeNeverImplicitlyGrantsOrPanics` |\n| `01M0TSGCWR0EVVQWK526A4BTEZ` expired try-lock context | barrier-controlled `TestEnsureRuntimeRoute_ConcurrentWritersUseOneCompleteWinner` plus canceled-waiter coverage |\n| `01M0TSEY7XNH32BR7ZXEGEMABS` revoke misses stale identity | both origin→path→origin and path→origin→path grant-ledger/revoke tests |\n| `01M0TSGEJB4B513AV3TS310RN0` disabled tier conflicts with `trust_all` | `TestEgressDecision_GlobalOffDeniesEvenWhenTrustAllIsTrue` |\n"},"started_at_ms":1787633090012,"completed_at_ms":1787633090012}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-25T04:45:20.024Z","ordinal":12839,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a0373c-b318-7a93-b6de-9b254c1ab7f6","call_id":"call_zO4Sset22lhXrZG4qnvDaEn9","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 30.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"### Task 4: Preserve and harden trust plus checkpoint egress\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/trust.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/trust_test.go`\n- Modify or delete after facade migration: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/trust.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/trust_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/trust_prompt.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/trust_prompt_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_push.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_sync_remote_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/trust_cmd.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/trust_cmd_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing trust-identity and ledger tests**\n\nCover:\n\n```go\nfunc TestEgressDecision_RequiresEveryFetchAndPushURL(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEgressDecision_UnparseableConfiguredOriginHolds(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEgressDecision_PathAppliesOnlyWhenOriginAbsent(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEgressDecision_GlobalOffDeniesEvenWhenTrustAllIsTrue(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestTrustGrant_OriginPathOriginRemovesOnlyRecordedStaleKeys(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestTrustRevoke_PathOriginPathRemovesEveryRecordedIdentity(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestTrustRevoke_PreservesHandAuthoredUnrelatedEntries(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEgressDecision_CommittedProjectSettingsNeverGrantConsent(t *testing.T)\n```\n\nStore the trust-grant ledger machine-locally under the same per-worktree registry. It records only keys written by CLI/prompt consent so hand-authored settings are not guessed or deleted.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Write failing pre-push behavior tests**\n\nPin all observable outcomes:\n\n```go\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_NoPendingCheckpointDoesNotPrompt(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_YesPersistsRepoTrustRechecksAndDrains(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_NotNowHoldsAndPushContinues(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_AlwaysPersistsTrustAllRechecksAndDrains(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_NonInteractiveHoldsWithoutReadingStdin(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_AccessibleModeNeverImplicitlyGrantsOrPanics(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestPrePushTrust_PromptOrWriteFailureHoldsWithoutFailingGitPush(t *testing.T)\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Run and verify failures**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'Test(EgressDecision|TrustGrant|TrustRevoke|PrePushTrust)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: FAIL on stale identity cleanup, accessible prompt handling, or the new policy API.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Implement one trust decision tree**\n\n`RepoPolicy.Trust` must carry state and source, not a reusable grant boolean:\n\n```go\ntype TrustDecision struct {\n\tAllowed bool\n\tSource  TrustSource\n\tReason  TrustReason\n\tIdentity TrustIdentity\n}\n```\n\nAfter Yes or Always persists consent, rerun `ClassifyRepoPolicy`; never continue using the pre-write decision. Every other egress entry point consumes the same decision without prompting.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Preserve the three-choice prompt safely**\n\nKeep the existing labels and effects. Read from `/dev/tty` through the repository interactive helper, never Git stdin. In accessible mode require an explicit supported choice; otherwise return held. Abort/error means Not now semantically, logs the operational failure, and does not fail the branch push.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Run focused trust and push tests**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy ./cmd/entire/cli/settings ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'Test(EgressDecision|Trust|Revoke|PrePush|CheckpointSync)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: PASS.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\n\nRun: `mise run check`\n\nCommit:\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy cmd/entire/cli/settings/trust.go cmd/entire/cli/settings/trust_test.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/trust_prompt.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/trust_prompt_test.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_push.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_sync_remote_test.go cmd/entire/cli/trust_cmd.go cmd/entire/cli/trust_cmd_test.go\ngit commit -m \"fix(global): preserve trust while hardening checkpoint egress\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 5: Make Claude and Gemini hook definitions declarative without changing behavior\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/user_hooks.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks_user.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks_user_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks_user.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks_user_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/setup_global.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/setup.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent_group.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent_group_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write contract tests before refactoring implementation**\n\nClaude must retain exactly these eight entries:\n\n```text\nSessionStart\nSessionEnd\nStop\nSubagentStop\nUserPromptSubmit\nPreToolUse[Agent]\nPostToolUse[Agent]\nPostToolUse[TaskCreate|TaskUpdate]\n```\n\nGemini must retain exactly twelve entries:\n\n```text\nSessionStart\nSessionEnd[exit]\nSessionEnd[logout]\nBeforeAgent\nAfterAgent\nBeforeModel\nAfterModel\nBeforeToolSelection\nBeforeTool[*]\nAfterTool[*]\nPreCompress\nNotification\n```\n\nTest both repo and user scopes, current production commands, matchers, unrelated-entry preservation, partial-install repair, legacy Entire-entry replacement, and cross-scope dedup assumptions.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run hook contract tests before changing code**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli -run 'Test.*Hooks' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: existing tests PASS; newly added exact-inventory tests provide the behavior baseline.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Introduce one declarative spec per agent**\n\nUse each agent's existing typed hook model. The spec must drive:\n\n- repo-scope installation;\n- user-scope installation;\n- currentness/completeness checks;\n- recognized Entire-entry removal;\n- expected counts for status/doctor.\n\nDo not create one lossy generic JSON schema across agents. Share orchestration, not agent-specific serialization.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Preserve no-op Gemini events**\n\nDo not remove `AfterModel`, `BeforeToolSelection`, `BeforeTool`, `AfterTool`, or `Notification`, even though their parser currently returns no lifecycle event. Their installed presence and command behavior are part of the product contract.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Reconcile hooks as infrastructure**\n\nUser-hook reconciliation runs only from installer/update integration\n(`curl-bash-post-install`), `entire enable`, `entire agent add`, and confirmed\ndoctor repair. `entire agent remove` removes that agent's user-scope Entire\nentries; repository disable/uninstall does not remove shared user-level\ninfrastructure. Reconciliation does not run inside hooks or read-only commands.\nInstallation errors warn without changing global activation policy.\n\nTarget only agents positively detected as installed or whose existing\nuser-scope configuration already contains an Entire entry; never create an\nabsent agent's config merely because its implementation is registered. Wrap\neach user config's read-modify-write in `flock.AcquireContext` with a named,\nbounded foreground timeout and keep the atomic lossless writer inside that\nlock. Add a concurrent-writer test proving unrelated user edits survive.\n\nAdd recursion suppression at the reconciliation coordinator: reject hook\ncontexts (`currentHookAgentName`/the hook command path) and propagate a private\n`ENTIRE_INTERNAL_USER_HOOK_RECONCILING=1` sentinel to child Entire processes.\nTests must prove a hook invocation and a child invocation make no config writes,\nwhile the four authorized foreground paths do.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Run agent tests and duplication check**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli ./cmd/entire/cli/agent -count=1\nmise run dup\n```\n\nExpected: exact inventory unchanged and repeated install/detect/remove loops eliminated or justified.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\n\nRun: `mise run check`\n\nCommit:\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/agent cmd/entire/cli/agent_group.go cmd/entire/cli/agent_group_test.go cmd/entire/cli/setup.go cmd/entire/cli/setup_global.go\ngit commit -m \"refactor(agents): declare user hook contracts once\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 6: Thread one policy snapshot through hooks and diagnostics\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/root.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/hook_registry.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/hook_registry_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/status.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/status_global_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/doctor.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/doctor_global_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/doctor_logs.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/doctor_bundle.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/config.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/global_warn.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/hook_settings_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/checkpoints.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/checkpoints_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/open.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint_backend_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_remote.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_sync_remote.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_hooks.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_push.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/hooks.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/common.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/unpushed_checkpoints.go`\n- Test: corresponding existing `_test.go` files for each hook-time consumer\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing single-classification tests**\n\nInject a counting classifier and assert one evaluation per process flow:\n\n```go\nfunc TestAgentHook_ClassifiesPolicyOnce(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestGitHook_ClassifiesPolicyOnce(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestStatus_ReadOnlyClassificationCreatesNoFiles(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestDoctor_ReadOnlyScanDoesNotMutatePolicyOrHooksWithoutConfirmation(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestHookPolicyFailureSkipsEntireWithoutFailingHostOperation(t *testing.T)\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run and verify failures**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'Test(AgentHook_ClassifiesPolicyOnce|GitHook_ClassifiesPolicyOnce|Status_ReadOnly|Doctor_ReadOnly|HookPolicyFailure)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: FAIL while consumers independently call settings gates and path probes.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Classify at hook entry and pass the snapshot through context**\n\nFor runtime-writing hooks:\n\n```go\np, err := repopolicy.ClassifyRepoPolicy(ctx)\nif err != nil || !p.Active { return nil }\np, err = repopolicy.EnsureRuntimeRoute(ctx, p)\nif err != nil { logAndSkip(); return nil }\nctx = repopolicy.WithRepoPolicy(ctx, p)\n```\n\nRemove migration-gate acquisition from agent and Git hook entry points. Route failure skips Entire work but not the user's agent, commit, or branch push.\n\nAfter storing the snapshot in context, make `settings.Load(ctx)` delegate to\n`LoadForRepoPolicy` whenever that context contains a policy. Audit every\nhook-reachable `settings.Load` call in `strategy/checkpoint_remote.go`,\n`strategy/checkpoint_sync_remote.go`, `strategy/manual_commit_hooks.go`,\n`strategy/manual_commit_push.go`, `strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go`,\n`strategy/hooks.go`, `strategy/common.go`, and lifecycle/state capture. Add\nconsumer-level tests proving malicious ignored values cannot select an OPF\ncommand, checkpoint remote/backend, external agent, hook path, signing mode, or\ncommit-linking behavior. Foreground commands running without a policy snapshot\nretain the existing full settings behavior.\n\nAudit the parallel checkpoint-config loader too. When context contains a\nglobal-only policy, `settings.LoadCheckpointsConfig` may honor explicit\n`ENTIRE_CHECKPOINTS_*` environment overrides but must not read repository\n`checkpoints` blocks; it returns nil so `checkpoint.Open`,\n`strategy/unpushed_checkpoints.go`, and all push/count paths select the compiled\ndefault backend. Add direct tests in `settings/checkpoints_test.go`, the\ncheckpoint open/backend tests, and the strategy consumer proving a malicious\nproject backend or mirror cannot be constructed. Local activation and\nforeground contexts without a policy retain existing checkpoint configuration.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Convert status and doctor to read-only policy consumers**\n\nStatus reports configured/enabled, settings path, activation source/reason, runtime layout, trust source/held state, and user-hook health. Doctor may repair hooks only on its confirmed repair path; ordinary status/help/auth/version invocations create no activation, route, setup, or agent-config files.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Preserve privacy-critical local failures**\n\nDo not blanket-swallow existing local OPF or redaction failures. Add a regression proving a local OPF safety failure still aborts push while policy/route/setup infrastructure failures do not.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Run focused hook/status/doctor tests**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy -run 'Test(AgentHook|GitHook|Lifecycle|Status|Doctor|HookPolicyFailure|OPF)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: PASS.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\n\nRun: `mise run check`\n\nCommit:\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/root.go cmd/entire/cli/hook_registry.go cmd/entire/cli/hook_registry_test.go cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd.go cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd_test.go cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle_test.go cmd/entire/cli/status.go cmd/entire/cli/status_global_test.go cmd/entire/cli/doctor.go cmd/entire/cli/doctor_global_test.go cmd/entire/cli/doctor_logs.go cmd/entire/cli/doctor_bundle.go cmd/entire/cli/config.go cmd/entire/cli/global_warn.go cmd/entire/cli/settings cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/open.go cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint_backend_test.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy\ngit commit -m \"refactor(global): share one policy snapshot across runtime paths\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 7: Add integration coverage, remove obsolete code, and prepare the coherent PR\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/global_enable_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/checkpoint_sync_remote_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_policy_test.go`\n- Modify: `docs/architecture/agent-integration-checklist.md`\n- Modify: `docs/security-and-privacy.md`\n- Modify: `CLAUDE.md`\n- Delete: obsolete migration-only tests/helpers identified by `rg`\n- Modify: any remaining user-facing source containing removed global-activation guidance\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Replace stacked integration tests with scenario tests**\n\nCreate real-binary integration coverage for:\n\n1. settings-file global activation -> Claude/Gemini user hook -> hidden runtime capture;\n2. no pending checkpoint -> no trust prompt/output;\n3. pending checkpoint -> Yes drains, Not now holds, Always drains all;\n4. non-interactive/accessible prompt paths hold safely without Git stdin reads;\n5. explicit enable after global capture keeps the git-common route;\n6. explicit-first route remains worktree-local after global settings turn on;\n7. fresh clone with committed `enabled: true` gains neither local activation nor egress;\n8. linked worktrees receive independent activation/route records;\n9. tracked or symlinked `.entire` cannot unlock executable settings or egress;\n10. multiple fetch/push URLs require complete trust.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run integration tests and verify failures before final fixes**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\nmise run test:integration\n```\n\nExpected: any remaining wiring gaps fail with a scenario name, not a low-level helper assertion.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Remove obsolete symbols and duplicated tests**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\nrg -n \"runEnableGlobalMode|runDisableGlobalMode|maybePromptGlobalTracking|maybeMigrateGlobalRuntimeData|migration gate|GlobalSetupCompleted|enable --global|disable --global\" --glob '!docs/superpowers/**'\n```\n\nExpected after cleanup: no production symbols or user-facing instructions remain. Historical changelog text may remain only when clearly historical and not presented as current usage.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Audit test quality and duplication**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\nmise run dup\nmise run lint:full\n```\n\nDelete tests that merely repeat implementation details; retain the policy matrix, race tests, security boundaries, exact hook inventories, and real-binary scenarios.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Measure the final diff budget**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngit diff --shortstat origin/main...HEAD\ngit diff --numstat origin/main...HEAD\n```\n\nTarget: approximately 8,000–10,000 additions total, 3,500–4,500 production additions, and materially more deletions than the current stacked branch. If additions remain near 13,000, perform another reuse/test-consolidation pass before landing.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Run final verification**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\nmise run check\nmise run lint\ngit diff --check\n```\n\nExpected: all PASS and worktree contains only intended source/test/doc changes. Do not run paid real-agent E2E tests.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Commit the integration and cleanup slice**\n\n```bash\ngit add CLAUDE.md cmd/entire/cli docs/architecture/agent-integration-checklist.md docs/security-and-privacy.md\ngit commit -m \"test(global): cover settings-only tracking end to end\"\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 8: Review the complete diff against `origin/main`**\n\nUse `entire:review` for intent-aware review, then `superpowers:requesting-code-review`. Address every valid finding and rerun the relevant focused test plus `mise run check` before any fixing commit.\n\n- [ ] **Step 9: Synthesize the clean PR history**\n\nKeep a local backup ref to the implementation branch. Rebuild the final PR head directly on `origin/main` as a coherent commit series or one reviewed squash commit; verify the rebuilt tree is byte-identical to the tested implementation tree before updating PR #2030. Do not preserve the old stack's merge commits or intermediate add-then-remove behavior.\n\n- [ ] **Step 10: Update the remote and close gates**\n\nBefore the authorized remote update, run `mise run lint` again. Update `feat/global-trust` with `--force-with-lease`, update the PR/trail body to describe the single coherent feature, then wait for every repository/PR gate to reach terminal state. Compare pre/post risk and security classifications, inspect every failure/degradation, fix valid findings, and repeat until stable. Resolve trail findings only after their implementation and regression tests are present remotely.\n\n## Finding closure checklist\n\nBefore resolving any trail finding, verify its named regression is present and\npassing:\n\n| Finding | Required regression |\n| --- | --- |\n| `01M0TSFS8WSCD7CNSV5XJ4Q983` migration gate blocks behind prompt/condensation | `TestPrePushTrust_*` plus concurrent route selection prove prompts/condensation run outside route locks |\n| `01M0TSFQ9D1EH7M7VCZ43FYVC6` gate failure aborts host operations | `TestHookPolicyFailureSkipsEntireWithoutFailingHostOperation` covers agent, commit, and branch push; local OPF failure still aborts |\n| `01M0TSEWA8GW6BMQEM98Y5AYMS` committed settings grant egress | `TestEgressDecision_CommittedProjectSettingsNeverGrantConsent` |\n| `01M0TSE2YQG4NHX4HQPK7P7FW6` symlinked `.entire` unlocks executable settings | provenance plus every hook-settings consumer test rejects symlink traversal and ignores executable/outbound fields |\n| `01M0TSDJQKTMR26TPV0Z1N7YG8` accessible prompt grants/panics | `TestPrePushTrust_AccessibleModeNeverImplicitlyGrantsOrPanics` |\n| `01M0TSGCWR0EVVQWK526A4BTEZ` expired try-lock context | barrier-controlled `TestEnsureRuntimeRoute_ConcurrentWritersUseOneCompleteWinner` plus canceled-waiter coverage |\n| `01M0TSEY7XNH32BR7ZXEGEMABS` revoke misses stale identity | both origin→path→origin and path→origin→path grant-ledger/revoke tests |\n| `01M0TSGEJB4B513AV3TS310RN0` disabled tier conflicts with `trust_all` | `TestEgressDecision_GlobalOffDeniesEvenWhenTrustAllIsTrue` |\n"}],"internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0371f-4feb-7263-aacd-7041d40b862c","create_time":1787633120.024208}}}
