{"timestamp":"2026-08-25T04:49:28.252Z","ordinal":12899,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a025ce-e754-7631-8467-eaa6035ba0f8","turn_id":"01a0371f-4feb-7263-aacd-7041d40b862c","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_068dffc2438c6825016a8d1ed6c1cc87d0905b190c66628adc","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\nTrust is now being made part of the immutable repository-policy snapshot, not a separate Boolean re-derived by each push/status caller. That prevents `trust_all` from accidentally overriding an inactive global tier and ensures all fetch and push URLs are evaluated together.\n\nThe machine-local ledger records only grants written by Entire, allowing identity transitions and revoke to remove stale CLI-owned keys without deleting unrelated hand-edited trust entries.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`"}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1787633366805,"completed_at_ms":1787633368252}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-25T04:49:28.253Z","ordinal":12900,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"msg_068dffc2438c6825016a8d1ed6c1cc87d0905b190c66628adc","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"output_text","text":"`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\nTrust is now being made part of the immutable repository-policy snapshot, not a separate Boolean re-derived by each push/status caller. That prevents `trust_all` from accidentally overriding an inactive global tier and ensures all fetch and push URLs are evaluated together.\n\nThe machine-local ledger records only grants written by Entire, allowing identity transitions and revoke to remove stale CLI-owned keys without deleting unrelated hand-edited trust entries.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`"}],"phase":"commentary","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0371f-4feb-7263-aacd-7041d40b862c","create_time":1787633347.959736}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-25T04:49:55.659Z","ordinal":12901,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_068dffc2438c6825016a8d1ed836e487d0b6707931d75b2933","status":"completed","call_id":"call_KYDcRQGCNQcj9HtTRZQQ0I5Z","name":"exec","input":"const patch = \"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/types.go\\n@@\\n-// TrustDecision is the repository's checkpoint-egress decision. Trust\\n-// identity and persistence are added independently of activation inputs.\\n+// TrustSource names the authority behind an egress decision.\\n+type TrustSource string\\n+\\n+const (\\n+\\tTrustSourceNone  TrustSource = \\\"none\\\"\\n+\\tTrustSourceLocal TrustSource = \\\"local_activation\\\"\\n+\\tTrustSourceAll   TrustSource = \\\"trust_all\\\"\\n+\\tTrustSourceRepo  TrustSource = \\\"repo\\\"\\n+)\\n+\\n+// TrustReason explains a held egress decision.\\n+type TrustReason string\\n+\\n+const (\\n+\\tTrustReasonNone          TrustReason = \\\"\\\"\\n+\\tTrustReasonInactive      TrustReason = \\\"inactive\\\"\\n+\\tTrustReasonUntrusted     TrustReason = \\\"untrusted\\\"\\n+\\tTrustReasonInvalidOrigin TrustReason = \\\"invalid_origin\\\"\\n+\\tTrustReasonSettings      TrustReason = \\\"settings_error\\\"\\n+)\\n+\\n+// TrustIdentity is the exclusive origin-or-path key used for egress consent.\\n+type TrustIdentity struct {\\n+\\tOriginKeys []string `json:\\\"origin_keys,omitempty\\\"`\\n+\\tPath       string   `json:\\\"path,omitempty\\\"`\\n+}\\n+\\n+// OriginKeyed reports whether this identity is remote-origin based.\\n+func (id TrustIdentity) OriginKeyed() bool { return len(id.OriginKeys) > 0 }\\n+\\n+// DisplayScope returns the user-facing identity scope.\\n+func (id TrustIdentity) DisplayScope() string {\\n+\\tif id.OriginKeyed() {\\n+\\t\\treturn id.OriginKeys[0]\\n+\\t}\\n+\\treturn id.Path\\n+}\\n+\\n+// TrustDecision is the repository's checkpoint-egress decision.\\n type TrustDecision struct {\\n-\\tAllowed bool\\n-\\tSource  string\\n+\\tAllowed  bool\\n+\\tSource   TrustSource\\n+\\tReason   TrustReason\\n+\\tIdentity TrustIdentity\\n }\\n*** Add File: /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/trust.go\\n+package repopolicy\\n+\\n+import (\\n+\\t\\\"context\\\"\\n+\\t\\\"errors\\\"\\n+\\t\\\"fmt\\\"\\n+\\t\\\"io/fs\\\"\\n+\\t\\\"os\\\"\\n+\\t\\\"path/filepath\\\"\\n+\\t\\\"slices\\\"\\n+\\t\\\"strings\\\"\\n+\\n+\\t\\\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/gitremote\\\"\\n+\\t\\\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/jsonutil\\\"\\n+)\\n+\\n+const trustLedgerFileName = \\\"trust.json\\\"\\n+\\n+// TrustGrantLedger tracks only consent keys written by Entire for this\\n+// worktree. It intentionally does not mirror hand-authored user settings.\\n+type TrustGrantLedger struct {\\n+\\tVersion            int      `json:\\\"version\\\"`\\n+\\tCanonicalWorktree  string   `json:\\\"canonical_worktree\\\"`\\n+\\tCanonicalGitCommon string   `json:\\\"canonical_git_common\\\"`\\n+\\tOriginKeys         []string `json:\\\"origin_keys,omitempty\\\"`\\n+\\tPaths              []string `json:\\\"paths,omitempty\\\"`\\n+}\\n+\\n+func trustLedgerPath(repository Repository) string {\\n+\\treturn filepath.Join(registryDir(repository), trustLedgerFileName)\\n+}\\n+\\n+// ResolveTrustIdentity derives an exclusive origin or path identity. A\\n+// configured but unparseable origin is an error; path identity is allowed only\\n+// when origin is absent.\\n+func ResolveTrustIdentity(ctx context.Context, repository Repository) (TrustIdentity, error) {\\n+\\turls, fetchFound, err := gitremote.GetRemoteURLsInDirIfSet(ctx, repository.WorktreeRoot, \\\"origin\\\")\\n+\\tif err != nil {\\n+\\t\\treturn TrustIdentity{}, fmt.Errorf(\\\"reading origin remote: %w\\\", err)\\n+\\t}\\n+\\tpushURLs, pushFound, err := gitremote.GetRemotePushURLsInDirIfSet(ctx, repository.WorktreeRoot, \\\"origin\\\")\\n+\\tif err != nil {\\n+\\t\\treturn TrustIdentity{}, fmt.Errorf(\\\"reading origin pushurl: %w\\\", err)\\n+\\t}\\n+\\turls = append(urls, pushURLs...)\\n+\\tif fetchFound || pushFound {\\n+\\t\\tkeys := make([]string, 0, len(urls))\\n+\\t\\tfor _, raw := range urls {\\n+\\t\\t\\tkey := NormalizeOrigin(raw)\\n+\\t\\t\\tif key == \\\"\\\" {\\n+\\t\\t\\t\\treturn TrustIdentity{}, errors.New(\\\"configured origin cannot be normalized\\\")\\n+\\t\\t\\t}\\n+\\t\\t\\tif !slices.Contains(keys, key) {\\n+\\t\\t\\t\\tkeys = append(keys, key)\\n+\\t\\t\\t}\\n+\\t\\t}\\n+\\t\\tif len(keys) == 0 {\\n+\\t\\t\\treturn TrustIdentity{}, errors.New(\\\"configured origin has no usable URLs\\\")\\n+\\t\\t}\\n+\\t\\treturn TrustIdentity{OriginKeys: keys}, nil\\n+\\t}\\n+\\treturn TrustIdentity{Path: repository.WorktreeRoot}, nil\\n+}\\n+\\n+// DecideEgress computes the single trust decision stored in RepoPolicy.\\n+func DecideEgress(ctx context.Context, policy RepoPolicy, global *GlobalConfig, repository Repository) TrustDecision {\\n+\\tif !policy.Active {\\n+\\t\\treturn TrustDecision{Source: TrustSourceNone, Reason: TrustReasonInactive}\\n+\\t}\\n+\\tif policy.ActivationSource == ActivationLocal {\\n+\\t\\treturn TrustDecision{Allowed: true, Source: TrustSourceLocal}\\n+\\t}\\n+\\tif global == nil || !global.Enabled {\\n+\\t\\treturn TrustDecision{Source: TrustSourceNone, Reason: TrustReasonInactive}\\n+\\t}\\n+\\tidentity, err := ResolveTrustIdentity(ctx, repository)\\n+\\tif err != nil {\\n+\\t\\treturn TrustDecision{Source: TrustSourceNone, Reason: TrustReasonInvalidOrigin}\\n+\\t}\\n+\\tdecision := TrustDecision{Source: TrustSourceNone, Reason: TrustReasonUntrusted, Identity: identity}\\n+\\tif global.TrustAll {\\n+\\t\\tdecision.Allowed = true\\n+\\t\\tdecision.Source = TrustSourceAll\\n+\\t\\tdecision.Reason = TrustReasonNone\\n+\\t\\treturn decision\\n+\\t}\\n+\\tif identityTrusted(ctx, global, identity) {\\n+\\t\\tdecision.Allowed = true\\n+\\t\\tdecision.Source = TrustSourceRepo\\n+\\t\\tdecision.Reason = TrustReasonNone\\n+\\t}\\n+\\treturn decision\\n+}\\n+\\n+func identityTrusted(ctx context.Context, global *GlobalConfig, identity TrustIdentity) bool {\\n+\\tif identity.OriginKeyed() {\\n+\\t\\tfor _, key := range identity.OriginKeys {\\n+\\t\\t\\tif !containsOrigin(global.TrustedOrigins, key) {\\n+\\t\\t\\t\\treturn false\\n+\\t\\t\\t}\\n+\\t\\t}\\n+\\t\\treturn true\\n+\\t}\\n+\\tmatched, err := MatchesExcludePathExact(ctx, global.TrustedPaths, identity.Path)\\n+\\treturn err == nil && matched\\n+}\\n+\\n+func containsOrigin(entries []string, key string) bool {\\n+\\tfor _, entry := range entries {\\n+\\t\\tif CanonicalTrustOrigin(entry) == key {\\n+\\t\\t\\treturn true\\n+\\t\\t}\\n+\\t}\\n+\\treturn false\\n+}\\n+\\n+// CanonicalTrustOrigin normalizes a hand-edited exact trust key.\\n+func CanonicalTrustOrigin(value string) string {\\n+\\treturn strings.ToLower(strings.TrimSpace(value))\\n+}\\n+\\n+// ReadTrustGrantLedger returns the verified machine-local grant history.\\n+func ReadTrustGrantLedger(repository Repository) (TrustGrantLedger, bool, error) {\\n+\\tif err := validateRepository(repository); err != nil {\\n+\\t\\treturn TrustGrantLedger{}, false, err\\n+\\t}\\n+\\tdata, err := os.ReadFile(trustLedgerPath(repository))\\n+\\tif err != nil {\\n+\\t\\tif errors.Is(err, fs.ErrNotExist) {\\n+\\t\\t\\treturn TrustGrantLedger{}, false, nil\\n+\\t\\t}\\n+\\t\\treturn TrustGrantLedger{}, false, fmt.Errorf(\\\"reading trust ledger: %w\\\", err)\\n+\\t}\\n+\\tvar ledger TrustGrantLedger\\n+\\tif err := decodeStrict(data, &ledger); err != nil {\\n+\\t\\treturn TrustGrantLedger{}, false, fmt.Errorf(\\\"parsing trust ledger: %w\\\", err)\\n+\\t}\\n+\\tif ledger.Version != recordVersion {\\n+\\t\\treturn TrustGrantLedger{}, false, fmt.Errorf(\\\"unsupported trust ledger version %d\\\", ledger.Version)\\n+\\t}\\n+\\tif ledger.CanonicalWorktree != repository.WorktreeRoot || ledger.CanonicalGitCommon != repository.GitCommonDir {\\n+\\t\\treturn TrustGrantLedger{}, false, errors.New(\\\"trust ledger repository identity mismatch\\\")\\n+\\t}\\n+\\treturn ledger, true, nil\\n+}\\n+\\n+// WriteTrustGrantLedger atomically records CLI-owned consent keys.\\n+func WriteTrustGrantLedger(repository Repository, ledger TrustGrantLedger) error {\\n+\\tif err := validateRepository(repository); err != nil {\\n+\\t\\treturn err\\n+\\t}\\n+\\tif err := ensureRegistryDir(repository); err != nil {\\n+\\t\\treturn err\\n+\\t}\\n+\\tledger.Version = recordVersion\\n+\\tledger.CanonicalWorktree = repository.WorktreeRoot\\n+\\tledger.CanonicalGitCommon = repository.GitCommonDir\\n+\\tdata, err := jsonutil.MarshalIndentWithNewline(ledger, \\\"\\\", \\\"  \\\")\\n+\\tif err != nil {\\n+\\t\\treturn fmt.Errorf(\\\"encoding trust ledger: %w\\\", err)\\n+\\t}\\n+\\tif err := jsonutil.WriteFileAtomic(trustLedgerPath(repository), data, 0o600); err != nil {\\n+\\t\\treturn fmt.Errorf(\\\"writing trust ledger: %w\\\", err)\\n+\\t}\\n+\\treturn nil\\n+}\\n*** Update File: /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/policy.go\\n@@\\n \\tif state == ActivationDisabled {\\n \\t\\tpolicy := policyForRepository(repository)\\n@@\\n-\\t\\treturn policy, nil\\n+\\t\\tpolicy.Trust = DecideEgress(ctx, policy, nil, repository)\\n+\\t\\treturn policy, nil\\n@@\\n-\\t\\treturn policy, nil\\n+\\t\\tpolicy.Trust = DecideEgress(ctx, policy, nil, repository)\\n+\\t\\treturn policy, nil\\n@@\\n \\tif state == ActivationEnabled {\\n@@\\n-\\t\\treturn policy, nil\\n+\\t\\tpolicy.Trust = DecideEgress(ctx, policy, nil, repository)\\n+\\t\\treturn policy, nil\\n@@\\n \\tif policy.Active {\\n@@\\n \\t} else {\\n@@\\n \\t}\\n+\\tpolicy.Trust = DecideEgress(ctx, policy, userSettings.Global, repository)\\n \\treturn policy, err\\n }\\n*** End Patch\";\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(patch));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0371f-4feb-7263-aacd-7041d40b862c","create_time":1787633347.959736}}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-25T04:49:56.053Z","ordinal":12902,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a025ce-e754-7631-8467-eaa6035ba0f8","turn_id":"01a0371f-4feb-7263-aacd-7041d40b862c","item":{"type":"FileChange","id":"exec-758c5b57-6b3a-4f9c-b9c3-51b9969982da","changes":{"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/types.go":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -41,7 +41,46 @@\n \n-// TrustDecision is the repository's checkpoint-egress decision. Trust\n-// identity and persistence are added independently of activation inputs.\n+// TrustSource names the authority behind an egress decision.\n+type TrustSource string\n+\n+const (\n+\tTrustSourceNone  TrustSource = \"none\"\n+\tTrustSourceLocal TrustSource = \"local_activation\"\n+\tTrustSourceAll   TrustSource = \"trust_all\"\n+\tTrustSourceRepo  TrustSource = \"repo\"\n+)\n+\n+// TrustReason explains a held egress decision.\n+type TrustReason string\n+\n+const (\n+\tTrustReasonNone          TrustReason = \"\"\n+\tTrustReasonInactive      TrustReason = \"inactive\"\n+\tTrustReasonUntrusted     TrustReason = \"untrusted\"\n+\tTrustReasonInvalidOrigin TrustReason = \"invalid_origin\"\n+\tTrustReasonSettings      TrustReason = \"settings_error\"\n+)\n+\n+// TrustIdentity is the exclusive origin-or-path key used for egress consent.\n+type TrustIdentity struct {\n+\tOriginKeys []string `json:\"origin_keys,omitempty\"`\n+\tPath       string   `json:\"path,omitempty\"`\n+}\n+\n+// OriginKeyed reports whether this identity is remote-origin based.\n+func (id TrustIdentity) OriginKeyed() bool { return len(id.OriginKeys) > 0 }\n+\n+// DisplayScope returns the user-facing identity scope.\n+func (id TrustIdentity) DisplayScope() string {\n+\tif id.OriginKeyed() {\n+\t\treturn id.OriginKeys[0]\n+\t}\n+\treturn id.Path\n+}\n+\n+// TrustDecision is the repository's checkpoint-egress decision.\n type TrustDecision struct {\n-\tAllowed bool\n-\tSource  string\n+\tAllowed  bool\n+\tSource   TrustSource\n+\tReason   TrustReason\n+\tIdentity TrustIdentity\n }\n","move_path":null},"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/trust.go":{"type":"add","content":"package repopolicy\n\nimport (\n\t\"context\"\n\t\"errors\"\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"io/fs\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\t\"slices\"\n\t\"strings\"\n\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/gitremote\"\n\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/jsonutil\"\n)\n\nconst trustLedgerFileName = \"trust.json\"\n\n// TrustGrantLedger tracks only consent keys written by Entire for this\n// worktree. It intentionally does not mirror hand-authored user settings.\ntype TrustGrantLedger struct {\n\tVersion            int      `json:\"version\"`\n\tCanonicalWorktree  string   `json:\"canonical_worktree\"`\n\tCanonicalGitCommon string   `json:\"canonical_git_common\"`\n\tOriginKeys         []string `json:\"origin_keys,omitempty\"`\n\tPaths              []string `json:\"paths,omitempty\"`\n}\n\nfunc trustLedgerPath(repository Repository) string {\n\treturn filepath.Join(registryDir(repository), trustLedgerFileName)\n}\n\n// ResolveTrustIdentity derives an exclusive origin or path identity. A\n// configured but unparseable origin is an error; path identity is allowed only\n// when origin is absent.\nfunc ResolveTrustIdentity(ctx context.Context, repository Repository) (TrustIdentity, error) {\n\turls, fetchFound, err := gitremote.GetRemoteURLsInDirIfSet(ctx, repository.WorktreeRoot, \"origin\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn TrustIdentity{}, fmt.Errorf(\"reading origin remote: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tpushURLs, pushFound, err := gitremote.GetRemotePushURLsInDirIfSet(ctx, repository.WorktreeRoot, \"origin\")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn TrustIdentity{}, fmt.Errorf(\"reading origin pushurl: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\turls = append(urls, pushURLs...)\n\tif fetchFound || pushFound {\n\t\tkeys := make([]string, 0, len(urls))\n\t\tfor _, raw := range urls {\n\t\t\tkey := NormalizeOrigin(raw)\n\t\t\tif key == \"\" {\n\t\t\t\treturn TrustIdentity{}, errors.New(\"configured origin cannot be normalized\")\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t\tif !slices.Contains(keys, key) {\n\t\t\t\tkeys = append(keys, key)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tif len(keys) == 0 {\n\t\t\treturn TrustIdentity{}, errors.New(\"configured origin has no usable URLs\")\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn TrustIdentity{OriginKeys: keys}, nil\n\t}\n\treturn TrustIdentity{Path: repository.WorktreeRoot}, nil\n}\n\n// DecideEgress computes the single trust decision stored in RepoPolicy.\nfunc DecideEgress(ctx context.Context, policy RepoPolicy, global *GlobalConfig, repository Repository) TrustDecision {\n\tif !policy.Active {\n\t\treturn TrustDecision{Source: TrustSourceNone, Reason: TrustReasonInactive}\n\t}\n\tif policy.ActivationSource == ActivationLocal {\n\t\treturn TrustDecision{Allowed: true, Source: TrustSourceLocal}\n\t}\n\tif global == nil || !global.Enabled {\n\t\treturn TrustDecision{Source: TrustSourceNone, Reason: TrustReasonInactive}\n\t}\n\tidentity, err := ResolveTrustIdentity(ctx, repository)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn TrustDecision{Source: TrustSourceNone, Reason: TrustReasonInvalidOrigin}\n\t}\n\tdecision := TrustDecision{Source: TrustSourceNone, Reason: TrustReasonUntrusted, Identity: identity}\n\tif global.TrustAll {\n\t\tdecision.Allowed = true\n\t\tdecision.Source = TrustSourceAll\n\t\tdecision.Reason = TrustReasonNone\n\t\treturn decision\n\t}\n\tif identityTrusted(ctx, global, identity) {\n\t\tdecision.Allowed = true\n\t\tdecision.Source = TrustSourceRepo\n\t\tdecision.Reason = TrustReasonNone\n\t}\n\treturn decision\n}\n\nfunc identityTrusted(ctx context.Context, global *GlobalConfig, identity TrustIdentity) bool {\n\tif identity.OriginKeyed() {\n\t\tfor _, key := range identity.OriginKeys {\n\t\t\tif !containsOrigin(global.TrustedOrigins, key) {\n\t\t\t\treturn false\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn true\n\t}\n\tmatched, err := MatchesExcludePathExact(ctx, global.TrustedPaths, identity.Path)\n\treturn err == nil && matched\n}\n\nfunc containsOrigin(entries []string, key string) bool {\n\tfor _, entry := range entries {\n\t\tif CanonicalTrustOrigin(entry) == key {\n\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false\n}\n\n// CanonicalTrustOrigin normalizes a hand-edited exact trust key.\nfunc CanonicalTrustOrigin(value string) string {\n\treturn strings.ToLower(strings.TrimSpace(value))\n}\n\n// ReadTrustGrantLedger returns the verified machine-local grant history.\nfunc ReadTrustGrantLedger(repository Repository) (TrustGrantLedger, bool, error) {\n\tif err := validateRepository(repository); err != nil {\n\t\treturn TrustGrantLedger{}, false, err\n\t}\n\tdata, err := os.ReadFile(trustLedgerPath(repository))\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tif errors.Is(err, fs.ErrNotExist) {\n\t\t\treturn TrustGrantLedger{}, false, nil\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn TrustGrantLedger{}, false, fmt.Errorf(\"reading trust ledger: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tvar ledger TrustGrantLedger\n\tif err := decodeStrict(data, &ledger); err != nil {\n\t\treturn TrustGrantLedger{}, false, fmt.Errorf(\"parsing trust ledger: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tif ledger.Version != recordVersion {\n\t\treturn TrustGrantLedger{}, false, fmt.Errorf(\"unsupported trust ledger version %d\", ledger.Version)\n\t}\n\tif ledger.CanonicalWorktree != repository.WorktreeRoot || ledger.CanonicalGitCommon != repository.GitCommonDir {\n\t\treturn TrustGrantLedger{}, false, errors.New(\"trust ledger repository identity mismatch\")\n\t}\n\treturn ledger, true, nil\n}\n\n// WriteTrustGrantLedger atomically records CLI-owned consent keys.\nfunc WriteTrustGrantLedger(repository Repository, ledger TrustGrantLedger) error {\n\tif err := validateRepository(repository); err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tif err := ensureRegistryDir(repository); err != nil {\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tledger.Version = recordVersion\n\tledger.CanonicalWorktree = repository.WorktreeRoot\n\tledger.CanonicalGitCommon = repository.GitCommonDir\n\tdata, err := jsonutil.MarshalIndentWithNewline(ledger, \"\", \"  \")\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"encoding trust ledger: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\tif err := jsonutil.WriteFileAtomic(trustLedgerPath(repository), data, 0o600); err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"writing trust ledger: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n"},"/Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/policy.go":{"type":"update","unified_diff":"@@ -34,2 +34,3 @@\n \t\tpolicy.Route = routeForClassification(repository, existingRoute, routeFound, RuntimeWorktree)\n+\t\tpolicy.Trust = DecideEgress(ctx, policy, nil, repository)\n \t\treturn policy, nil\n@@ -45,2 +46,3 @@\n \t\tpolicy.Route = routeForClassification(repository, existingRoute, routeFound, RuntimeWorktree)\n+\t\tpolicy.Trust = DecideEgress(ctx, policy, nil, repository)\n \t\treturn policy, nil\n@@ -52,2 +54,3 @@\n \t\tpolicy.Route = routeForClassification(repository, existingRoute, routeFound, RuntimeWorktree)\n+\t\tpolicy.Trust = DecideEgress(ctx, policy, nil, repository)\n \t\treturn policy, nil\n@@ -72,2 +75,3 @@\n \t}\n+\tpolicy.Trust = DecideEgress(ctx, policy, userSettings.Global, repository)\n \treturn policy, err\n","move_path":null}},"status":"completed","stdout":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/trust.go\nM /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/types.go\nM /Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents - Peyton’s MacBook Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier/cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/policy.go\n","stderr":""},"started_at_ms":1787633395818,"completed_at_ms":1787633396052}}
