{"timestamp":"2026-08-25T04:58:01.300Z","ordinal":13032,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a025ce-e754-7631-8467-eaa6035ba0f8","turn_id":"01a0371f-4feb-7263-aacd-7041d40b862c","item":{"type":"CommandExecution","id":"exec-55599f91-7984-446a-baf4-c497fdd9f7cc","process_id":"9222","command":["/bin/zsh","-lc","sed -n '1,320p' docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor.md"],"cwd":"file:///Users/peytonmontei/Documents/Documents%20-%20Peyton%E2%80%99s%20MacBook%20Pro/entire/devenv/entireio/cli/.worktrees/global-settings-tier","parsed_cmd":[{"type":"read","cmd":"sed -n '1,320p' docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor.md","name":"2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor.md","path":"docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-24-settings-only-global-tracking-refactor.md"}],"source":"unified_exec_startup","status":"completed","stdout":"# Settings-Only Global Tracking Refactor Implementation Plan\n\n> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.\n\n**Goal:** Replace the stacked global-enable implementation with one coherent policy-and-routing architecture while preserving pre-push trust, checkpoint egress, and the complete Claude Code and Gemini CLI hook behavior.\n\n**Architecture:** A leaf package under `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy` owns user-global settings, repository policy classification, machine-local activation, immutable runtime routing, and trust identity. Existing `settings` APIs become compatibility facades while consumers migrate to one immutable `RepoPolicy` snapshot. Runtime routing is sticky per worktree, lazy setup is component-versioned, and the old enable/wizard/takeover migration paths are deleted.\n\n**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26, Cobra, Charm `huh`, go-git v6, repository `flock` and `jsonutil` helpers, table-driven Go tests, integration-tag tests, Vogon deterministic E2E canary.\n\n---\n\n## Scope and execution notes\n\n- Work in the existing dedicated `global-settings-tier` worktree.\n- Preserve `bca00205a` and branch `fix/global-takeover-migration` as the stacked reference while refactoring.\n- The design and this plan are local artifacts under ignored `docs/superpowers`; do not add or commit them.\n- Do not run real-agent E2E tests. `mise run check` runs only the approved deterministic canaries.\n- Before writing Go in each task, search for reusable helpers with `rg` because the documented `/go:discover-related` skill is not installed in this environment.\n- Every top-level test and subtest uses `t.Parallel()` unless it calls `t.Chdir`, `t.Setenv`, or modifies another process-global seam.\n- Every Git-touching test uses `testutil.InitRepo`, repository-local identity/GPG config, and a temp worktree.\n- Before every commit run `mise run check`. Before any push rerun `mise run lint` after the final formatter pass.\n- Recorded intent from Entire checkpoints and commit history that must survive:\n  - the disabled/unconfigured global fast path performs no Git subprocess;\n  - invalid exclusions fail closed;\n  - global-only tracking never writes `.entire/metadata`, `logs`, or `tmp` into the worktree;\n  - lazy setup never turns an agent/Git hook failure into a failed host operation;\n  - pre-push consent remains Yes / Not now / Always and Git stdin is never used;\n  - Claude/Gemini user-hook installs preserve unrelated configuration and deduplicate against repo-scope production hooks.\n\n## Final file structure\n\n### New leaf policy package\n\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/types.go`: immutable policy, activation, route, trust, and reason types.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/user_settings.go`: strict user settings schema, loading, validation, locking, and atomic writes.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/repository.go`: Git/worktree facts and stable worktree namespace resolution without importing `paths` or parent `settings`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/activation.go`: project-settings provenance, activation marker, legacy bootstrap, and disable tombstone.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/route.go`: route registry, atomic first-writer-wins selection, and policy context memo.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/policy.go`: read-only `ClassifyRepoPolicy` and mutating `EnsureRuntimeRoute` orchestration.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/trust.go`: trust identity, egress decision, trust writers, and grant ledger.\n- Matching focused `_test.go` files beside each responsibility.\n\n### Existing packages\n\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/global.go`: shrink to aliases/facades plus public diagnostics helpers; no independent policy tree.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/hook_settings.go`: convert verified provenance into a positive-whitelist `EntireSettings` view for hook-time consumers.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/trust.go`: shrink to compatibility facades or delete once callers use `repopolicy`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/paths/invisible.go`: construct runtime paths from a resolved route; delete settings parsing and activation mirrors.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/setup_global.go`: retain user-hook reconciliation helpers only; delete global activation commands, wizard, and runtime migration.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/global_setup.go`: component-versioned lazy Git setup consuming `RepoPolicy`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/{claudecode,geminicli}/hooks*.go`: declarative hook specs shared by repo/user install, detection, removal, and diagnostics.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/{root,hook_registry,hooks_git_cmd,lifecycle,status,doctor,setup}.go`: resolve/pass one policy snapshot and preserve user surfaces.\n\n---\n\n### Task 1: Establish the leaf policy model and user-settings authority\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/types.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/user_settings.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/user_settings_test.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/repository.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/repository_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/global.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/global_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/global_validate.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Search for reusable primitives and record the dependency boundary**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\nrg -n \"ModifyUserSettings|WriteFileAtomicFollowingSymlinks|Normalize.*Origin|GetRemoteURLsInDirIfSet|GetRemotePushURLsInDirIfSet|HashWorktreeID|GetWorktreeID\" cmd/entire/cli internal\n```\n\nExpected: reuse `jsonutil` atomic writes, `flock`, `gitremote`, and the existing worktree-ID algorithm; `repopolicy` must not import `paths`, parent `settings`, `session`, `strategy`, or `logging`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Write failing schema and fast-path tests**\n\nCover:\n\n```go\nfunc TestLoadUserSettings_MissingMalformedAndStrict(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestClassifyGlobalConfig_DisabledDoesNotResolveRepository(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestValidateGlobalConfig_InvalidExclusionsFailClosed(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestModifyUserSettings_ConcurrentTrustWritesDoNotClobber(t *testing.T)\n```\n\nThe disabled/unconfigured test injects a repository resolver that fails the test if called.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Run the tests and verify they fail for the missing package**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy -run 'Test(LoadUserSettings|ClassifyGlobalConfig|ValidateGlobalConfig|ModifyUserSettings)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: FAIL because the new APIs do not exist.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Implement the minimal immutable types and settings store**\n\nUse these public shapes:\n\n```go\ntype ActivationSource string\n\nconst (\n\tActivationInactive ActivationSource = \"inactive\"\n\tActivationLocal    ActivationSource = \"local\"\n\tActivationGlobal   ActivationSource = \"global\"\n)\n\ntype RuntimeLayout string\n\nconst (\n\tRuntimeUnknown   RuntimeLayout = \"\"\n\tRuntimeWorktree  RuntimeLayout = \"worktree\"\n\tRuntimeGitCommon RuntimeLayout = \"git_common\"\n)\n\ntype RepoPolicy struct {\n\tActive           bool\n\tActivationSource ActivationSource\n\tInactiveReason   InactiveReason\n\tWorktreeRoot     string\n\tGitCommonDir     string\n\tWorktreeKey      string\n\tRoute            RuntimeRoute\n\tTrust            TrustDecision\n}\n\ntype UserSettings struct {\n\tGlobal *GlobalConfig `json:\"global,omitempty\"`\n}\n```\n\nKeep the existing JSON field names and strict decoding. Keep `ModifyUserSettings` as the only writer primitive and clear only package-owned memos after persistence.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Convert the parent settings package to aliases/facades**\n\nThe facade should preserve current call sites during migration:\n\n```go\ntype GlobalConfig = repopolicy.GlobalConfig\ntype UserSettings = repopolicy.UserSettings\n\nfunc LoadUserSettings(ctx context.Context) (*UserSettings, error) {\n\treturn repopolicy.LoadUserSettings(ctx)\n}\n\nfunc ModifyUserSettings(ctx context.Context, fn func(*UserSettings) error) error {\n\treturn repopolicy.ModifyUserSettings(ctx, fn)\n}\n```\n\nMove validation and normalization into the leaf package instead of leaving a second implementation in `settings`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Run focused and parent-package tests**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy ./cmd/entire/cli/settings -run 'Test(Global|LoadUserSettings|ModifyUserSettings|ValidateGlobal)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: PASS.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\n\nRun: `mise run check`\n\nExpected: formatting, lint, unit/integration tests, and deterministic canaries PASS.\n\nCommit:\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy cmd/entire/cli/settings/global.go cmd/entire/cli/settings/global_test.go cmd/entire/cli/settings/global_validate.go\ngit commit -m \"refactor(settings): centralize global repository policy inputs\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 2: Add machine-local activation provenance and sticky runtime routing\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/activation.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/activation_test.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/provenance.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/provenance_test.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/hook_settings.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/hook_settings_test.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/route.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/route_test.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/policy.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/policy_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/paths/invisible.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/paths/invisible_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/paths/paths.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/paths/worktree.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing activation-provenance tests**\n\nCover the exact matrix:\n\n```go\nfunc TestClassifyRepoPolicy_CommittedEnabledSettingDoesNotActivateFreshClone(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestClassifyRepoPolicy_LocalMarkerActivatesOnlyItsWorktree(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestClassifyRepoPolicy_DisabledMarkerVetoesGlobalActivation(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestBootstrapLegacyActivation_SingleWorktreeRequiresVerifiedEvidence(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestBootstrapLegacyActivation_LinkedWorktreeRejectsSharedHookEvidence(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestBootstrapLegacyActivation_RejectsTrackedOrSymlinkedEvidence(t *testing.T)\n```\n\nAccepted legacy evidence is only an exact-worktree active session record or one of the recognized, untracked, non-symlinked `.entire/metadata/<session-id>/` files named in the spec.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run the activation tests and verify failure**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy -run 'Test(ClassifyRepoPolicy|BootstrapLegacyActivation)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: FAIL because activation records are not implemented.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Implement activation records**\n\nStore one record per worktree at:\n\n```text\n<git-common-dir>/entire/worktree/<worktree-key>/activation.json\n```\n\nUse a versioned record:\n\n```go\ntype ActivationRecord struct {\n\tVersion            int             `json:\"version\"`\n\tState              ActivationState `json:\"state\"`\n\tCanonicalWorktree  string          `json:\"canonical_worktree\"`\n\tCanonicalGitCommon string          `json:\"canonical_git_common\"`\n}\n```\n\nWrites are atomic `0600` files under the same `0700` per-worktree registry and\nare machine-local. Each record carries and verifies the full canonical\nworktree/Git-common identities in addition to its schema version and state.\n`entire enable` writes `enabled`; `entire disable` writes `disabled`; corrupt,\nunknown-version, or identity-mismatched records fail closed and are recoverable\nonly through explicit enable.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Write failing hook-settings provenance tests**\n\nThe leaf package reports verified local-settings provenance; the parent\n`settings` package builds the typed sanitized view so it can preserve the exact\nexisting field shapes. Cover a fresh clone whose tracked or symlink-traversing `.entire` contains\nmalicious values for OPF commands, checkpoint destination, external agents,\nabsolute hook path, strategy options, commit linking, signing, and Vercel.\nUnder global-only activation none may influence hook execution or egress.\nBuilt-in declarative redaction remains available, and locally activated\nrepositories retain the existing per-field provenance behavior.\n\nSpecify the intended API in the test:\n\n```go\nfunc LoadForRepoPolicy(ctx context.Context, p repopolicy.RepoPolicy) (*EntireSettings, error)\n```\n\nFor global-only activation the returned `EntireSettings` copies only\n`enabled`, `log_level`, `redaction.pii` (including category pointers and\n`custom_patterns`), `redaction.custom_redactions` as its existing\n`map[string]string`, and `redaction.externalize_images`. It reconstructs the\nredaction object rather than copying scanner/OPF substructures. Malformed\nallowed fields fail closed. Local activation preserves the current merged\nloader and OPF command provenance rule.\n\nAdd an exhaustive reflection-backed test over every JSON field of\n`EntireSettings` and `RedactionSettings`: each field must appear in an explicit\nallowed-or-ignored classification table, so adding a field cannot expose it to\nglobal hooks by accident.\n\nValidation starts at the canonical worktree root and `lstat`s each\nworktree-relative `.entire/settings*.json` path component. Never derive the\nrelative path from an already attacker-controlled symlink target.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Run the provenance tests and verify failure**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy ./cmd/entire/cli/settings -run 'Test.*(Provenance|LoadForRepoPolicy|HookFieldClassification)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: FAIL before the provenance validator and sanitized loader exist.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Implement the hook-settings provenance boundary**\n\nImplement the typed API and exhaustive classification described in Step 4,\nusing the leaf package only for path/provenance decisions and the parent\n`settings` package for `EntireSettings` construction.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Write failing route-selection tests**\n\nCover:\n\n```go\nfunc TestEnsureRuntimeRoute_GlobalFirstSelectsGitCommonAndStaysThere(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEnsureRuntimeRoute_ExplicitFirstSelectsWorktreeAndStaysThere(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEnsureRuntimeRoute_ConcurrentWritersUseOneCompleteWinner(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEnsureRuntimeRoute_CanceledWaiterDoesNotPoisonWinner(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEnsureRuntimeRoute_LinkedWorktreesAreIndependent(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestClassifyRepoPolicy_ReadOnlyDoesNotCreateRegistry(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestEnsureRuntimeRoute_CorruptRecordFailsClosed(t *testing.T)\n```\n\n- [ ] **Step 8: Implement first-writer-wins route records**\n\nStore:\n","stderr":"","aggregated_output":"# Settings-Only Global Tracking Refactor Implementation Plan\n\n> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.\n\n**Goal:** Replace the stacked global-enable implementation with one coherent policy-and-routing architecture while preserving pre-push trust, checkpoint egress, and the complete Claude Code and Gemini CLI hook behavior.\n\n**Architecture:** A leaf package under `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy` owns user-global settings, repository policy classification, machine-local activation, immutable runtime routing, and trust identity. Existing `settings` APIs become compatibility facades while consumers migrate to one immutable `RepoPolicy` snapshot. Runtime routing is sticky per worktree, lazy setup is component-versioned, and the old enable/wizard/takeover migration paths are deleted.\n\n**Tech Stack:** Go 1.26, Cobra, Charm `huh`, go-git v6, repository `flock` and `jsonutil` helpers, table-driven Go tests, integration-tag tests, Vogon deterministic E2E canary.\n\n---\n\n## Scope and execution notes\n\n- Work in the existing dedicated `global-settings-tier` worktree.\n- Preserve `bca00205a` and branch `fix/global-takeover-migration` as the stacked reference while refactoring.\n- The design and this plan are local artifacts under ignored `docs/superpowers`; do not add or commit them.\n- Do not run real-agent E2E tests. `mise run check` runs only the approved deterministic canaries.\n- Before writing Go in each task, search for reusable helpers with `rg` because the documented `/go:discover-related` skill is not installed in this environment.\n- Every top-level test and subtest uses `t.Parallel()` unless it calls `t.Chdir`, `t.Setenv`, or modifies another process-global seam.\n- Every Git-touching test uses `testutil.InitRepo`, repository-local identity/GPG config, and a temp worktree.\n- Before every commit run `mise run check`. Before any push rerun `mise run lint` after the final formatter pass.\n- Recorded intent from Entire checkpoints and commit history that must survive:\n  - the disabled/unconfigured global fast path performs no Git subprocess;\n  - invalid exclusions fail closed;\n  - global-only tracking never writes `.entire/metadata`, `logs`, or `tmp` into the worktree;\n  - lazy setup never turns an agent/Git hook failure into a failed host operation;\n  - pre-push consent remains Yes / Not now / Always and Git stdin is never used;\n  - Claude/Gemini user-hook installs preserve unrelated configuration and deduplicate against repo-scope production hooks.\n\n## Final file structure\n\n### New leaf policy package\n\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/types.go`: immutable policy, activation, route, trust, and reason types.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/user_settings.go`: strict user settings schema, loading, validation, locking, and atomic writes.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/repository.go`: Git/worktree facts and stable worktree namespace resolution without importing `paths` or parent `settings`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/activation.go`: project-settings provenance, activation marker, legacy bootstrap, and disable tombstone.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/route.go`: route registry, atomic first-writer-wins selection, and policy context memo.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/policy.go`: read-only `ClassifyRepoPolicy` and mutating `EnsureRuntimeRoute` orchestration.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/trust.go`: trust identity, egress decision, trust writers, and grant ledger.\n- Matching focused `_test.go` files beside each responsibility.\n\n### Existing packages\n\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/global.go`: shrink to aliases/facades plus public diagnostics helpers; no independent policy tree.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/hook_settings.go`: convert verified provenance into a positive-whitelist `EntireSettings` view for hook-time consumers.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/trust.go`: shrink to compatibility facades or delete once callers use `repopolicy`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/paths/invisible.go`: construct runtime paths from a resolved route; delete settings parsing and activation mirrors.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/setup_global.go`: retain user-hook reconciliation helpers only; delete global activation commands, wizard, and runtime migration.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/global_setup.go`: component-versioned lazy Git setup consuming `RepoPolicy`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/{claudecode,geminicli}/hooks*.go`: declarative hook specs shared by repo/user install, detection, removal, and diagnostics.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/{root,hook_registry,hooks_git_cmd,lifecycle,status,doctor,setup}.go`: resolve/pass one policy snapshot and preserve user surfaces.\n\n---\n\n### Task 1: Establish the leaf policy model and user-settings authority\n\n**Files:**\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/types.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/user_settings.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/user_settings_test.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/repository.go`\n- Create: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy/repository_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/global.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/global_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/global_validate.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Search for reusable primitives and record the dependency boundary**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\nrg -n \"ModifyUserSettings|WriteFileAtomicFollowingSymlinks|Normalize.*Origin|GetRemoteURLsInDirIfSet|GetRemotePushURLsInDirIfSet|HashWorktreeID|GetWorktreeID\" cmd/entire/cli internal\n```\n\nExpected: reuse `jsonutil` atomic writes, `flock`, `gitremote`, and the existing worktree-ID algorithm; `repopolicy` must not import `paths`, parent `settings`, `session`, `strategy`, or `logging`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Write failing schema and fast-path tests**\n\nCover:\n\n```go\nfunc TestLoadUs