``\n\n---\n\n### Task 5: Make Claude and Gemini hook definitions declarative without changing behavior\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/user_hooks.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks_user.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode/hooks_user_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks_user.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli/hooks_user_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/setup_global.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/setup.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent_group.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/agent_group_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write contract tests before refactoring implementation**\n\nClaude must retain exactly these eight entries:\n\n```text\nSessionStart\nSessionEnd\nStop\nSubagentStop\nUserPromptSubmit\nPreToolUse[Agent]\nPostToolUse[Agent]\nPostToolUse[TaskCreate|TaskUpdate]\n```\n\nGemini must retain exactly twelve entries:\n\n```text\nSessionStart\nSessionEnd[exit]\nSessionEnd[logout]\nBeforeAgent\nAfterAgent\nBeforeModel\nAfterModel\nBeforeToolSelection\nBeforeTool[*]\nAfterTool[*]\nPreCompress\nNotification\n```\n\nTest both repo and user scopes, current production commands, matchers, unrelated-entry preservation, partial-install repair, legacy Entire-entry replacement, and cross-scope dedup assumptions.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run hook contract tests before changing code**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli -run 'Test.*Hooks' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: existing tests PASS; newly added exact-inventory tests provide the behavior baseline.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Introduce one declarative spec per agent**\n\nUse each agent's existing typed hook model. The spec must drive:\n\n- repo-scope installation;\n- user-scope installation;\n- currentness/completeness checks;\n- recognized Entire-entry removal;\n- expected counts for status/doctor.\n\nDo not create one lossy generic JSON schema across agents. Share orchestration, not agent-specific serialization.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Preserve no-op Gemini events**\n\nDo not remove `AfterModel`, `BeforeToolSelection`, `BeforeTool`, `AfterTool`, or `Notification`, even though their parser currently returns no lifecycle event. Their installed presence and command behavior are part of the product contract.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Reconcile hooks as infrastructure**\n\nUser-hook reconciliation runs only from installer/update integration\n(`curl-bash-post-install`), `entire enable`, `entire agent add`, and confirmed\ndoctor repair. `entire agent remove` removes that agent's user-scope Entire\nentries; repository disable/uninstall does not remove shared user-level\ninfrastructure. Reconciliation does not run inside hooks or read-only commands.\nInstallation errors warn without changing global activation policy.\n\nTarget only agents positively detected as installed or whose existing\nuser-scope configuration already contains an Entire entry; never create an\nabsent agent's config merely because its implementation is registered. Wrap\neach user config's read-modify-write in `flock.AcquireContext` with a named,\nbounded foreground timeout and keep the atomic lossless writer inside that\nlock. Add a concurrent-writer test proving unrelated user edits survive.\n\nAdd recursion suppression at the reconciliation coordinator: reject hook\ncontexts (`currentHookAgentName`/the hook command path) and propagate a private\n`ENTIRE_INTERNAL_USER_HOOK_RECONCILING=1` sentinel to child Entire processes.\nTests must prove a hook invocation and a child invocation make no config writes,\nwhile the four authorized foreground paths do.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Run agent tests and duplication check**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/geminicli ./cmd/entire/cli/agent -count=1\nmise run dup\n```\n\nExpected: exact inventory unchanged and repeated install/detect/remove loops eliminated or justified.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\n\nRun: `mise run check`\n\nCommit:\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/agent cmd/entire/cli/agent_group.go cmd/entire/cli/agent_group_test.go cmd/entire/cli/setup.go cmd/entire/cli/setup_global.go\ngit commit -m \"refactor(agents): declare user hook contracts once\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 6: Thread one policy snapshot through hooks and diagnostics\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/root.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/hook_registry.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/hook_registry_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/hooks_git_cmd_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/lifecycle_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/status.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/status_global_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/doctor.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/doctor_global_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/doctor_logs.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/doctor_bundle.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/config.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/global_warn.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/hook_settings_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/checkpoints.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/checkpoints_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/open.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint_backend_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_remote.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/checkpoint_sync_remote.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_hooks.go`\n"},"started_at_ms":1787633891110,"completed_at_ms":1787633891110}}
{"timestamp":"2026-08-25T04:58:17.138Z","ordinal":13039,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call_output","id":"ctco_01a03748-8eb2-7f43-9b84-7287d24ab014","call_id":"call_0hgEhwCS863al3MtRQ7RLuQ0","output":[{"type":"input_text","text":"Script completed\nWall time 6.1 seconds\nOutput:\n"},{"type":"input_text","text":"Store:\n\n```text\n<git-common-dir>/entire/worktree/<worktree-key>/route.json\n```\n\nUse:\n\n```go\ntype RuntimeRoute struct {\n\tVersion           int           `json:\"version\"`\n\tLayout            RuntimeLayout `json:\"layout\"`\n\tCanonicalWorktree string        `json:\"canonical_worktree\"`\n\tCanonicalGitCommon string       `json:\"canonical_git_common\"`\n}\n\nfunc ClassifyRepoPolicy(ctx context.Context) (RepoPolicy, error)\nfunc EnsureRuntimeRoute(ctx context.Context, p RepoPolicy) (RepoPolicy, error)\nfunc WithRepoPolicy(ctx context.Context, p RepoPolicy) context.Context\nfunc RepoPolicyFromContext(ctx context.Context) (RepoPolicy, bool)\n```\n\nThe creation critical section covers only read/create/publish. Write and fsync\na complete `0600` temp file beneath a user-owned `0700` registry directory,\npublish without replacing an existing record, then reread the winner. On every\nread verify the full canonical worktree and Git-common identities before using\nthe short-hash namespace; a mismatch fails closed. Never hold this lock around\nhooks, prompts, Git operations, condensation, or runtime writes.\n\n- [ ] **Step 9: Reduce `paths` to route consumption**\n\n`paths.AbsPath` should obtain a policy snapshot from context or call read-only classification as a compatibility fallback, then map only `metadata`, `logs`, and `tmp` through the selected route. Delete `repoActivationConfigured`, `userGlobalTierEnabled`, and duplicated JSON/settings parsing from `paths/invisible.go`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 10: Run focused route/path tests**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy ./cmd/entire/cli/settings ./cmd/entire/cli/paths -run 'Test(EnsureRuntimeRoute|ClassifyRepoPolicy|BootstrapLegacyActivation|LoadForRepoPolicy|Invisible|AbsPath)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: PASS, including cancellation and separate-git-dir coverage.\n\n- [ ] **Step 11: Run duplication checks before commit**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\nmise run dup\n```\n\nExpected: no new actionable duplication between `repopolicy` and `paths`.\n\n- [ ] **Step 12: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\n\nRun: `mise run check`\n\nCommit:\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/settings/repopolicy cmd/entire/cli/settings/hook_settings.go cmd/entire/cli/settings/hook_settings_test.go cmd/entire/cli/paths\ngit commit -m \"refactor(global): make activation and runtime routing sticky\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 3: Remove global activation commands, wizard, and takeover migration\n\n**Files:**\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/setup.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/setup_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/setup_global.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/setup_global_test.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/root.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/root_test.go` if present; otherwise the nearest root/help test file\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/global_setup.go`\n- Modify: `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/global_setup_test.go`\n\n- [ ] **Step 1: Write failing command-surface tests**\n\nAdd tests asserting:\n\n```go\nfunc TestEnableCommand_HasNoGlobalFlag(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestDisableCommand_HasNoGlobalFlag(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestSetupFlow_DoesNotAskGlobalTrackingQuestion(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestRootHelp_DoesNotAdvertiseGlobalActivationFlags(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestUserFacingStrings_DoNotReferenceRemovedGlobalFlags(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestUninstall_RemovesOnlyCurrentWorktreeRuntimeAndRefs(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestUninstall_PreservesSharedGitHooksForActiveSibling(t *testing.T)\nfunc TestUninstall_NeverRemovesUserLevelAgentHooks(t *testing.T)\n```\n\nThe repository-wide string test scans user-facing Go strings and docs but excludes historical specs/checkpoints.\n\n- [ ] **Step 2: Run and observe failures against the current stack**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli -run 'Test(EnableCommand_HasNoGlobalFlag|DisableCommand_HasNoGlobalFlag|SetupFlow_DoesNotAskGlobalTrackingQuestion|RootHelp_DoesNotAdvertiseGlobalActivationFlags|UserFacingStrings)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: FAIL on flags, wizard, hints, doctor text, and docs.\n\n- [ ] **Step 3: Delete activation mutation surfaces**\n\nRemove:\n\n- `runEnableGlobalMode` and `runDisableGlobalMode`;\n- both `--global` flags and mutual-exclusion wiring;\n- `maybePromptGlobalTracking`, configured/unconfigured ask-once state, and global tracking hints;\n- every user message telling the user to run either removed flag.\n\nDo not remove `entire trust`, `entire trust --revoke`, or the pre-push trust prompt.\n\n- [ ] **Step 4: Delete takeover migration**\n\nRemove from `setup_global.go` and callers:\n\n- migration planning and traversal;\n- migration lock/gate;\n- file move/copy helpers introduced solely for takeover;\n- transcript path rewriting;\n- retry/marker clearing used only to trigger migration.\n\nKeep generic atomic JSON helpers and any independently used hook-install lock.\n\n- [ ] **Step 5: Wire explicit enable/disable to activation and route**\n\nThe order for `entire enable` is:\n\n```go\nerr := persistRepoSettingsWithoutRuntimeRouting(...)\np, err := repopolicy.ClassifyRepoPolicy(ctx)\np, err = repopolicy.EnsureRuntimeRoute(ctx, p)\nerr = repopolicy.SetLocalActivation(ctx, repopolicy.ActivationEnabled)\n```\n\nThe settings write is deliberately rooted at the literal worktree and does not\ncall `paths.AbsPath`; a project settings file is configuration, never runtime\ndata. Use the routed policy context for subsequent setup. On partial failure,\nreturn an actionable error and leave capture fail-closed. `entire disable`\nrecords a per-worktree disabled marker and preserves the route; `--uninstall`\nremoves only the current worktree's runtime/route data but retains the disabled\ntombstone.\n\nBefore changing uninstall, add linked-worktree tests with one active sibling.\nSession-state deletion and shadow-branch deletion must be filtered to the\ncurrent worktree key; the sibling's state, runtime registry, route, activation,\nand shadow branches survive. Repository-scope agent hooks and `.entire` cleanup\ntarget only the current worktree. Shared Git hooks are removed only when no\nother worktree in the clone remains locally or globally active. User-level\nClaude/Gemini hooks are infrastructure and are never removed by repository\ndisable/uninstall.\n\n- [ ] **Step 6: Replace the clone-wide setup boolean with component state**\n\nReplace `ClonePreferences.GlobalSetupCompleted` with a per-worktree component record under the registry, for example:\n\n```go\ntype SetupRecord struct {\n\tVersion       int `json:\"version\"`\n\tGitHooksSpec  int `json:\"git_hooks_spec\"`\n\tPrimaryRefSpec int `json:\"primary_ref_spec\"`\n}\n```\n\n`MaybeEnsureGlobalSetup` repairs only stale/missing components, remains silent inside hooks, and does not mark an unsafe worktree-resident `core.hooksPath` as installed.\n\n- [ ] **Step 7: Run focused setup tests**\n\nRun:\n\n```bash\ngo test ./cmd/entire/cli ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy -run 'Test(Enable|Disable|Uninstall|SetupFlow|RootHelp|UserFacingStrings|MaybeEnsureGlobalSetup|EnsureSetupForHook)' -count=1\n```\n\nExpected: PASS; no migration tests or symbols remain.\n\n- [ ] **Step 8: Run the required pre-commit gate and commit**\n\nRun: `mise run check`\n\nCommit:\n\n```bash\ngit add cmd/entire/cli/setup.go cmd/entire/cli/setup_test.go cmd/entire/cli/setup_global.go cmd/entire/cli/setup_global_test.go cmd/entire/cli/root.go cmd/entire/cli/root_test.go cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/global_setup.go cmd/entire/cli/strategy/global_setup_test.go\ngit commit -m \"refactor(global): make activation settings-only\"\n```\n\n---\n\n### Task 4