{"timestamp":"2026-08-25T05:02:19.308Z","ordinal":13160,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a025ce-e754-7631-8467-eaa6035ba0f8","turn_id":"01a0371f-4feb-7263-aacd-7041d40b862c","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_068dffc2438c6825016a8d21d9af3087d0bc312cfc08e5705b","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\nThe trust ledger records only keys written by Entire, not the whole trust configuration. That lets identity changes remove stale CLI grants while preserving hand-authored trust entries—especially important when a repository moves between path-only and origin-based identity.\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────`\n\nThe trust/egress focused suites now pass. I’m formatting and running the required repository gate before committing this slice, then I’ll move directly into the Claude/Gemini contract cleanup."}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1787634137714,"completed_at_ms":1787634139308}}
