sting() is false in the subprocess, so the\n    30\t\t// internal/testdirs fallback cannot protect it — isolation must come from\n    31\t\t// the environment, which children inherit because all integration env\n    32\t\t// building starts from os.Environ() (testutil.GitIsolatedEnv).\n    33\t\t//\n    34\t\t// GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0 and ENTIRE_TEST_GIT_HERMETIC form the hermeticity\n    35\t\t// tripwire: the latter makes GitIsolatedEnv's global git config route HTTPS\n    36\t\t// transport to real external hosts (github.com, gitlab.com) through a dead\n    37\t\t// loopback proxy, so any test whose git commands accidentally dial the network\n    38\t\t// fails fast instead of reaching it or prompting for credentials (regressions\n    39\t\t// #1463, 53bc37a88). The config lives in the file because GitIsolatedEnv strips\n    40\t\t// inherited GIT_CONFIG_* env; it proxies transport only (not url.insteadOf, which\n    41\t\t// would corrupt origin-URL forge detection) and leaves loopback servers untouched.\n    42\t\tisolation := map[string]string{\n    43\t\t\t\"ENTIRE_CONFIG_DIR\":           filepath.Join(tmpDir, \"entire-config\"),\n    44\t\t\t\"XDG_CACHE_HOME\":              filepath.Join(tmpDir, \"entire-cache\"),\n    45\t\t\t\"ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE\":          \"file\",\n    46\t\t\t\"ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE_PATH\":     filepath.Join(tmpDir, \"entire-tokens.json\"),\n    47\t\t\t\"ENTIRE_TEST_AUTH_STORE_FILE\": filepath.Join(tmpDir, \"entire-auth-tokens.json\"),\n    48\t\t\t\"GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT\":         \"0\",\n    49\t\t\ttestutil.EnvGitHermetic:       \"1\",\n    50\t\t\t// Plugin fixtures are file:// repos, which the shipped allowlist\n    51\t\t\t// refuses — nothing in production needs a local git remote, and a\n    52\t\t\t// security allowlist should not be widened for test convenience.\n    53\t\t\t// testing.Testing() is false in the spawned binary, so it is told here.\n    54\t\t\t\"ENTIRE_TEST_ALLOW_FILE_REMOTES\": \"1\",\n    55\t\t}\n    56\t\tfor 