{"timestamp":"2026-08-25T16:51:29.491Z","ordinal":14573,"type":"event_msg","payload":{"type":"item_completed","thread_id":"01a025ce-e754-7631-8467-eaa6035ba0f8","turn_id":"01a039b7-b242-7af0-80e0-d29bf9afbbac","item":{"type":"AgentMessage","id":"msg_068dffc2438c6825016a8dc810276487d095e311f70007fba5","content":[{"type":"Text","text":"`★ Insight ─────────────────────────────────────`\n- The local-only failure is another incomplete hand-built fixture: it claims to simulate `enable --local` but omits the new activation record.\n- The rename failure is different: identity-bound activation correctly rejects copied records, so relocation must be reauthorized only through verified same-session evidence—not by accepting any mismatched record.\n`─────────────────────────────────────────────────`"}],"phase":"commentary"},"started_at_ms":1787676688192,"completed_at_ms":1787676689491}}
